<i>Music, dairy products,
coffee, TV shows...</i>

252
00:11:21.139 --> 00:11:24.459
<i>surveillance systems, all
history books, voting machines.</i>

253
00:11:24.601 --> 00:11:25.372
Wait a minute.

254
00:11:25.852 --> 00:11:28.080
Come on, you can't be this stupid.

255
00:11:28.229 --> 00:11:29.706
This is a misunderstanding.

256
00:11:29.856 --> 00:11:31.754
I'm just a regular,
normal, ordinary guy.

257
00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:34.094
I'm late to meet my best
friends in the whole world.

258
00:11:34.235 --> 00:11:35.131
They're probably
missing me right now.

259
00:11:35.278 --> 00:11:36.846
They're probably out
looking around.

260
00:11:36.988 --> 00:11:39.289
"Hey, where's Emmet? Hey,
where's my best friend Emmet?"

261
00:11:39.365 --> 00:11:41.718
Hey, you know what? Ask all
my friends. They'll tell you.

262
00:11:42.327 --> 00:11:44.646
Oh, we asked them, all right.

263
00:11:44.787 --> 00:11:45.729
Boom!

264
00:11:45.872 --> 00:11:48.066
<i>That guy's not a
criminal mastermind.</i>

265
00:11:48.208 --> 00:11:49.104
See?

266
00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:52.775
<i>Yeah. You know, he's kind of an
average, normal kind of guy.</i>

267
00:11:52.921 --> 00:11:53.943
Thank you.

268
00:11:54.088 --> 00:11:54.905
<i>But, you know, he's not, like...</i>

269
00:11:55.048 --> 00:11:57.321
<i>normal like us. No.</i>

270
00:11:57.467 --> 00:12:00.286
<i>He's not that special.</i>

271
00:12:00.428 --> 00:12:03.281
<i>Wait, I'm so confused.
Who are we talking about?</i>

272
00:12:05.099 --> 00:12:06.496
<i>Wait, does he work with us?</i>

273
00:12:06.643 --> 00:12:08.086
Gail doesn't remember me?

274
00:12:08.228 --> 00:12:09.204
<i>Look at Randy here.</i>

275
00:12:09.354 --> 00:12:11.957
<i>He likes sausage. That's something.</i>

276
00:12:12.106 --> 00:12:14.755
<i>Gail is perky. That's something.</i>

277
00:12:14.901 --> 00:12:15.547
<i>And Harry...</i>

278
00:12:15.693 --> 00:12:17.966
<i>- well...
- When you say Harry, I go:</i>

279
00:12:19.906 --> 00:12:22.600
<i>When you say the other guy, I go:</i>

280
00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:24.761
<i>Harry's the best!</i>

281
00:12:24.911 --> 00:12:27.139
<i>- Harry's got personality.
- He's weird! He's weird!</i>

282
00:12:27.288 --> 00:12:30.562
<i>I know that guy but I know,
like, zippy-zap about him.</i>

283
00:12:30.708 --> 00:12:32.276
We just talked earlier.

284
00:12:32.418 --> 00:12:34.316
<i>I mean, all he does is say yes...</i>

285
00:12:34.462 --> 00:12:36.610
<i>to everything everybody
else is doing.</i>

286
00:12:36.756 --> 00:12:38.984
<i>You know, he's just
sort of a "Hmm!"</i>

287
00:12:39.133 --> 00:12:41.952
<i>Little bit of a blank
slate, I guess.</i>

288
00:12:42.512 --> 00:12:44.990
<i>That'll be $42, please.</i>

289
00:12:45.139 --> 00:12:49.210
<i>We all have something that makes
us something and Emmet is...</i>

290
00:12:51.562 --> 00:12:52.834
<i>nothing.</i>

291
00:12:54.524 --> 00:12:55.967
There you go.

292
00:12:56.526 --> 00:12:59.220
- I told you I was a nobody.
- Oh.

293
00:12:59.362 --> 00:13:01.009
It's the perfect cover.

294
00:13:01.155 --> 00:13:02.928
Cover? Cover for what?

295
00:13:03.074 --> 00:13:05.768
I can't break him. Take him
to the melting chamber.

296
00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.853
What? Aah!

297
00:13:10.915 --> 00:13:13.234
You're gonna melt me?
Am I gonna die?

298
00:13:13.376 --> 00:13:14.819
You'll live. You'll be fine.

299
00:13:16.129 --> 00:13:18.527
President Business.
I have him right here, sir.

300
00:13:18.673 --> 00:13:22.744
Yes, we've told him he'll live so he
doesn't try to escape, but, um...

301
00:13:22.885 --> 00:13:24.237
we're lying to him.

302
00:13:24.387 --> 00:13:25.989
Wait, what did he just say?

303
00:13:26.139 --> 00:13:27.161
Hold still.

304
00:13:27.307 --> 00:13:30.331
Wait! There's obviously been a
mix-up here. You've got the wrong...

305
00:13:30.476 --> 00:13:32.374
Ow! Ow, ow, ow!

306
00:13:33.688 --> 00:13:35.210
That is gonna start hurting...

307
00:13:35.356 --> 00:13:36.503
pretty soon.

308
00:13:59.881 --> 00:14:01.449
Ow, ow, ow!

309
00:14:04.844 --> 00:14:05.615
No, no, no!

310
00:14:08.097 --> 00:14:09.949
Whoa. Who are you?

311
00:14:14.187 --> 00:14:15.709
It's you?

312
00:14:15.855 --> 00:14:17.707
Come with me if you wanna not die.

313
00:14:21.235 --> 00:14:23.337
Hi, everybody!
How's the melting goi...?

314
00:14:23.488 --> 00:14:24.259
Hey, hey, hey!

315
00:14:25.323 --> 00:14:26.345
Red alert, red alert.

316
00:14:26.491 --> 00:14:30.061
I need everyone, repeat: everyone,
to go after The Special.

317
00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:33.431
The tunnel's that way.

318
00:14:35.166 --> 00:14:36.518
Oh, boy!

319
00:14:37.085 --> 00:14:38.357
Oh, sir, you're brilliant.

320
00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:42.365
- We'll build a motorcycle out of the alleyway.
- Ow. Oh.

321
00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.543
So, uh, didn't catch your name...

322
00:14:54.936 --> 00:14:58.131
or anything about what
you're, uh, up to.

323
00:14:58.272 --> 00:14:59.794
Or what we're doing here.

324
00:14:59.941 --> 00:15:02.601
It's brilliant, sir, that you
pretended to be a useless nobody...

325
00:15:02.944 --> 00:15:05.172
but you can drop the act
with me. It's cool.

326
00:15:05.321 --> 00:15:06.889
Oh, the act.

327
00:15:07.281 --> 00:15:08.507
Whoa.

328
00:15:10.535 --> 00:15:11.602
Whoa!

329
00:15:11.744 --> 00:15:13.562
Jump on. Let's go!

330
00:15:18.209 --> 00:15:20.482
- Hey, uh, I...
- Hang on, sir.

331
00:15:20.628 --> 00:15:21.570
All units...

332
00:15:21.712 --> 00:15:23.530
cut him off on Elm, now!

333
00:15:23.673 --> 00:15:24.899
Or whenever you can.

334
00:15:25.049 --> 00:15:26.492
<i>10-4, Bad Cop.</i>

335
00:15:26.634 --> 00:15:28.031
- Watch out!
- Hold on.

336
00:15:31.305 --> 00:15:32.497
We need to meet up
with Vitruvius...

337
00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.520
- and tell him the Piece has been found.
- Uh-huh.

338
00:15:34.559 --> 00:15:35.976
They're up on the monorail.

339
00:15:35.977 --> 00:15:37.545
Release the copper choppers.

340
00:15:46.487 --> 00:15:47.554
Oh, no!

341
00:15:49.323 --> 00:15:51.517
Will you please tell
me what is happening?

342
00:15:51.701 --> 00:15:54.224
I'm rescuing you, sir. You're
the one the prophecy spoke of.

343
00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:55.312
You're The Special.

344
00:15:55.788 --> 00:15:56.480
Me?

345
00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:00.609
You found the Piece of Resistance.

346
00:16:00.751 --> 00:16:02.148
And the prophecy states...

347
00:16:02.295 --> 00:16:04.568
that you are the most
important, most talented...

348
00:16:04.714 --> 00:16:05.940
most interesting...

349
00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:10.195
and most extraordinary
person in the universe.

350
00:16:10.761 --> 00:16:12.238
That's you. Right?

351
00:16:13.389 --> 00:16:16.618
Uh, yes. That's me.

352
00:16:16.767 --> 00:16:17.834
Great. You drive.

353
00:16:17.977 --> 00:16:18.578
What?

354
00:16:27.653 --> 00:16:28.970
I wanna go home!

355
00:16:30.698 --> 00:16:31.799
This is not what I meant!

356
00:16:40.833 --> 00:16:41.614
Oh, no.

357
00:16:41.751 --> 00:16:42.647
Look out, Special!

358
00:16:42.793 --> 00:16:45.487
Uh, sorry. Never driven
a motorcycle. Sorry!

359
00:16:49.342 --> 00:16:50.864
- Wow, he's amazing.
- Aah!

360
00:16:56.224 --> 00:16:57.450
That was incredible!

361
00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:59.953
You're even better than the
prophecy said you'd be.

362
00:17:00.102 --> 00:17:01.374
Oh. Really?

363
00:17:01.521 --> 00:17:03.248
I'm, uh... I'm Wyldstyle.

364
00:17:03.397 --> 00:17:05.249
- Oh, I'm sorry, what was it?
- Wyldstyle.

365
00:17:05.399 --> 00:17:06.733
- "Wyldstyle"?
- Yep.

366
00:17:06.734 --> 00:17:07.881
- What are you, a DJ?
- No.

367
00:17:08.027 --> 00:17:10.175
- Oh, that's your name? "Wyldstyle"?
- Yeah.

368
00:17:10.321 --> 00:17:11.968
Like on your birth certificate,
it says "Wyldstyle."

369
00:17:12.114 --> 00:17:12.885
Let's not talk about my name!

370
00:17:13.032 --> 00:17:14.509
Don't let The Special get away.

371
00:17:14.659 --> 00:17:15.899
Sir, we've blocked the freeway.

372
00:17:16.077 --> 00:17:17.224
Hang on, sir!

373
00:17:17.995 --> 00:17:19.096
What are you doing?

374
00:17:21.082 --> 00:17:21.933
Let's fly!

375
00:17:22.083 --> 00:17:23.935
Whoa!

376
00:17:24.085 --> 00:17:25.732
Head for the secret tunnel.

377
00:17:25.878 --> 00:17:27.418
Uh, these are the city limits.

378
00:17:27.421 --> 00:17:29.161
Let's just head for the tunnel.

379
00:17:29.715 --> 00:17:31.408
You want me to drive into
that weird swirly hole?

380
00:17:31.551 --> 00:17:32.251
Are you insane?

381
00:17:32.385 --> 00:17:34.203
Don't brake! Go!
Don't stop! Go! Now!

382
00:17:34.345 --> 00:17:35.287
I can't do this!

383
00:17:35.429 --> 00:17:37.952
That is against the instructions!

384
00:17:39.183 --> 00:17:40.830
Wait, what's your
favorite restaurant?

385
00:17:40.977 --> 00:17:41.917
Any chain restaurant.

386
00:17:42.019 --> 00:17:42.769
Favorite TV show?

387
00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:43.371
<i>Where Are My Pants?</i>

388
00:17:43.521 --> 00:17:44.182
Favorite song?

389
00:17:44.272 --> 00:17:45.532
<i>Everything Is Awesome</i>

390
00:17:45.565 --> 00:17:46.666
Oh, no!

391
00:17:55.283 --> 00:17:58.057
Darn, darn, darn, darny-darn!

392
00:18:37.241 --> 00:18:39.435
Wait. Where are we?

393
00:18:41.829 --> 00:18:43.522
This is so weir...! Ow!

394
00:18:43.664 --> 00:18:45.812
You're not The Special!
You lied to me!

395
00:18:45.958 --> 00:18:47.685
It really kind of depends on...

396
00:18:47.835 --> 00:18:49.575
You're not even a
MasterBuilder, are you?

397
00:18:49.712 --> 00:18:51.906
Uh, I mean, I know what
a MasterBuilder is.

398
00:18:52.048 --> 00:18:55.118
Why don't you tell me what it is?
That way I could see if you're right.

399
00:18:55.259 --> 00:18:57.612
You've ruined the prophecy.

400
00:18:58.512 --> 00:19:01.115
Look, I'm sorry, okay? You just...

401
00:19:01.265 --> 00:19:03.584
You made being special
sound so good.

402
00:19:03.726 --> 00:19:06.579
And to think I was going to follow
you to the end of the universe.

403
00:19:07.271 --> 00:19:08.623
You were?

404
00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:10.086
Here's the thing.

405
00:19:10.232 --> 00:19:12.835
How do we know for sure
that I'm not The Special?

406
00:19:12.985 --> 00:19:14.553
- We just don't know it yet.
- Quiet.

407
00:19:14.695 --> 00:19:16.388
Y'all want a giant turkey leg?

408
00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:18.598
Do you have any idea what
that does to your colon?

409
00:19:20.868 --> 00:19:23.972
- Oh, my G-O-S-H.
- Just put the hat on.

410
00:19:24.121 --> 00:19:24.847
Oh...

411
00:19:24.997 --> 00:19:26.770
and this. And this. And this.

412
00:19:26.916 --> 00:19:28.563
- And this.
- Aah!

413
00:19:28.709 --> 00:19:30.436
And, by the way,
I have a boyfriend.

414
00:19:30.628 --> 00:19:32.776
Uh, I'm not sure exactly
why you'd bring that up.

415
00:19:32.922 --> 00:19:33.944
It's super serious.

416
00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:35.612
You do not want to mess with him.

417
00:19:35.758 --> 00:19:36.359
Okay.

418
00:19:36.509 --> 00:19:37.781
So don't get any ideas.

419
00:19:37.927 --> 00:19:39.700
I never have any ideas.

420
00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:41.372
Wait!

421
00:19:41.514 --> 00:19:43.662
- Stick them up.
- Hands where I can see them.

422
00:19:43.808 --> 00:19:46.988
Hey, uh, listen. You think you can
explain why I'm dressed like this...

423
00:19:47.019 --> 00:19:48.587
and what those big words
in the sky were all about?

424
00:19:48.729 --> 00:19:51.298
And, like, where we are in time.

425
00:19:53.693 --> 00:19:56.633
Your home, Bricksburg, is one
of many realms in the universe.

426
00:19:56.737 --> 00:19:57.797
There's also this one...

427
00:19:57.905 --> 00:20:00.490
<i>Pirate's Cove, Knight's Club,
Viking's Landing, Clown Town...</i>

428
00:20:00.491 --> 00:20:01.808
<i>a bunch of others we
don't need to mention.</i>

429
00:20:01.951 --> 00:20:02.643
Mm-hm.

430
00:20:02.785 --> 00:20:04.686
Lord Business, or as you
think you know him...

431
00:20:04.745 --> 00:20:05.971
President Business...

432
00:20:06.122 --> 00:20:09.066
stole the Kragle, the most
powerful object in the universe.

433
00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:10.977
Blah, blah, blah.

434
00:20:11.127 --> 00:20:14.026
Proper name. Place name.
Backstory stuff.

435
00:20:14.171 --> 00:20:16.490
- ...Piece of Resistance is The Special.
- Mm-hm.

436
00:20:16.632 --> 00:20:19.110
I'm so pretty. I like you.

437
00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.658
But I'm angry with
you for some reason.

438
00:20:21.804 --> 00:20:23.156
- ...tower at the end of the universe...
- Mm-hm.

439
00:20:23.305 --> 00:20:25.265
put the Piece of Resistance
onto the Kragle...

440
00:20:25.266 --> 00:20:26.993
and disarm it forever.

441
00:20:27.143 --> 00:20:28.210
Great.

442
00:20:28.352 --> 00:20:29.499
I think I got it...

443
00:20:29.645 --> 00:20:30.792
but just in case...

444
00:20:30.938 --> 00:20:32.898
tell me the whole thing again.
I wasn't listening.

445
00:20:34.817 --> 00:20:38.171
<i>Okay. All the people of the universe
were once free to travel...</i>

446
00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:41.390
<i>and mingle and build
whatever they wanted.</i>

447
00:20:41.532 --> 00:20:43.760
<i>But President Business was
confused by all the chaos.</i>

448
00:20:44.744 --> 00:20:46.596
<i>So he erected walls
between the worlds...</i>

449
00:20:46.746 --> 00:20:49.520
<i>and became obsessed with
order and perfection.</i>

450
00:20:49.665 --> 00:20:51.142
<i>And he stole the mysterious...</i>

451
00:20:51.292 --> 00:20:53.235
<i>- secret super weapon called...</i>
- The Kragle!

452
00:20:53.377 --> 00:20:54.794
<i>And he hired Bad Cop...</i>

453
00:20:54.795 --> 00:20:57.895
<i>to hunt down all the MasterBuilders,
who were always changing everything.</i>

454
00:20:58.424 --> 00:20:59.776
<i>And those of us who remained...</i>

455
00:20:59.925 --> 00:21:03.655
<i>well, we went into hiding.
Built the tunnels to survive.</i>

456
00:21:03.804 --> 00:21:05.584
And we search for the
Piece of Resistance.

457
00:21:05.723 --> 00:21:08.417
The only thing that
can stop the Kragle.

458
00:21:08.559 --> 00:21:09.831
Kragle. I know that.

459
00:21:09.977 --> 00:21:12.125
It might have been that cop.
He said something about the Kragle.

460
00:21:12.271 --> 00:21:14.544
President Business was
going to use the Kragle...

461
00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:16.151
to end the world in three days.

462
00:21:16.192 --> 00:21:17.452
I can't make any sense of it.

463
00:21:17.485 --> 00:21:18.677
Taco Tuesday.

464
00:21:18.819 --> 00:21:21.092
I knew that was suspicious.
There's no time to lose.

465
00:21:21.238 --> 00:21:24.308
We must find Vitruvius and get to the
Office Tower before it's too late.

466
00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:25.551
Okay.

467
00:21:25.701 --> 00:21:27.929
Heh. How scary can
someone's office be?

468
00:21:37.087 --> 00:21:39.468
President Business, we're trying
to locate the fugitive...

469
00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.990
but his face is so generic it matches
every other face in our database.

470
00:21:43.135 --> 00:21:44.782
Diabolical.

471
00:21:44.929 --> 00:21:47.999
Okay, have Bad Cop meet
me in my office...

472
00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:49.841
- ...in 23 seconds. Ciao.
- Will do, sir.

473
00:21:49.934 --> 00:21:51.832
Coffee sales are
through the roof, sir.

474
00:21:51.977 --> 00:21:54.397
Glad to hear it. Let's rebuild
that roof to be even higher!

475
00:21:54.522 --> 00:21:55.748
The roof team is on it.

476
00:21:55.898 --> 00:21:58.217
Sir, can you approve this
poster for Taco Tuesday?

477
00:21:58.359 --> 00:21:59.506
Perfect. Whoo!

478
00:21:59.652 --> 00:22:01.652
- I love everyone in this room.
- We love you, sir!

479
00:22:01.654 --> 00:22:04.177
- Great job on the radio station.
- Thank you, sir.

480
00:22:04.323 --> 00:22:06.471
We love listening to this
song over and over again.

481
00:22:06.617 --> 00:22:07.513
Keep it up, guys.

482
00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:09.762
Honey, where are my...

483
00:22:09.912 --> 00:22:11.079
- pants?
- Ha-ha-ha!

484
00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:12.227
Cut! Ha, ha!

485
00:22:12.373 --> 00:22:14.100
Hilarious. That never gets old.

486
00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:15.272
It does not.

487
00:22:15.417 --> 00:22:17.861
Bad Cop is waiting for
you in your office.

488
00:22:18.003 --> 00:22:19.355
Wonderful. Fantastic.

489
00:22:19.505 --> 00:22:21.403
Would you cancel my 2:00?

490
00:22:21.549 --> 00:22:23.777
This next meeting could
run a little bit...

491
00:22:23.926 --> 00:22:25.027
deadly.

492
00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:34.002
<i>Activate helmet.</i>

493
00:22:35.187 --> 00:22:36.584
<i>Light sequence.</i>

494
00:22:36.730 --> 00:22:37.547
<i>Flame test.</i>

495
00:22:38.983 --> 00:22:40.644
<i>- Engage dramatic entrance.</i>
- Aah!

496
00:22:40.734 --> 00:22:42.051
Bad Cop.

497
00:22:42.194 --> 00:22:44.296
Lord Business. I know The
Special got away, but...

498
00:22:44.446 --> 00:22:46.298
Don't be so serious.

499
00:22:46.448 --> 00:22:47.674
Where's the other guy?

500
00:22:47.825 --> 00:22:49.768
- Hey, friend.
- Hey, buddy!

501
00:22:49.910 --> 00:22:51.762
- I missed you.
- Aw, did you really?

502
00:22:51.912 --> 00:22:53.663
Have I ever shown you
my relic collection?

503
00:22:53.664 --> 00:22:54.936
Nope. I don't think you have.

504
00:22:55.082 --> 00:22:56.822
Nobody knows where
this stuff comes from.

505
00:22:56.917 --> 00:22:57.893
This one...

506
00:22:58.043 --> 00:22:59.611
is the Cloak of Ban Da'ld.

507
00:22:59.753 --> 00:23:01.337
I hear it's super
painful to take off.

508
00:23:01.338 --> 00:23:02.985
- You wanna try it on?
- Well, um...

509
00:23:03.132 --> 00:23:04.700
No, but thank you.

510
00:23:04.842 --> 00:23:07.445
We've done some great work over
the years together, Bad Cop...

511
00:23:07.595 --> 00:23:09.572
capturing all those
MasterBuilders...

512
00:23:09.722 --> 00:23:11.449
and torturing them and whatnot.

513
00:23:11.599 --> 00:23:12.416
Thank you, sir.

514
00:23:12.558 --> 00:23:13.705
Although...

515
00:23:13.851 --> 00:23:15.435
you did let the Piece
of Resistance go.

516
00:23:15.436 --> 00:23:17.163
The one thing that
can ruin my plans.

517
00:23:17.313 --> 00:23:19.733
The one thing that I asked
you to take care of.

518
00:23:20.274 --> 00:23:21.967
That's super frustrating.

519
00:23:22.109 --> 00:23:24.928
It makes me just wanna
pick up whoever...

520
00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:26.968
is standing closest to me...

521
00:23:27.114 --> 00:23:28.932
and throw them through
this window...

522
00:23:29.074 --> 00:23:32.849
and out into the infinite
abyss of nothingness!

523
00:23:35.831 --> 00:23:37.774
I wanna do it so bad.

524
00:23:37.917 --> 00:23:40.065
I know you do, sir. Please don't.

525
00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:43.610
And it's not just you, Bad Cop,
that keeps messing up my plans.

526
00:23:43.756 --> 00:23:47.486
People everywhere are always
messing with my stuff.

527
00:23:47.885 --> 00:23:50.579
But I have a way to fix that.

528
00:23:50.763 --> 00:23:54.242
A way to keep things exactly the
way they are supposed to be.

529
00:23:54.934 --> 00:23:56.581
Permanently.

530
00:23:56.727 --> 00:23:58.420
<i>Behold...</i>

531
00:23:58.646 --> 00:24:00.589
<i>the most powerful weapon...</i>

532
00:24:00.731 --> 00:24:02.333
<i>of all the relics:</i>

533
00:24:03.359 --> 00:24:05.803
<i>The Kragle!</i>

534
00:24:10.199 --> 00:24:13.409
As you can see, they're loading the
Kragle in a big machine upstairs.

535
00:24:13.410 --> 00:24:14.306
I call it...

536
00:24:14.453 --> 00:24:17.056
the Tentacle Arm Kragle
Outside Sprayer.

537
00:24:17.206 --> 00:24:18.603
Or TAKOS.

538
00:24:18.749 --> 00:24:20.066
The "S" is silent.

539
00:24:20.209 --> 00:24:22.653
So on Taco Tuesday...

540
00:24:22.795 --> 00:24:25.068
it's going to spray the Kragle
over everyone and everything...

541
00:24:25.214 --> 00:24:28.693
with a bunch of super-scary
nozzles like this one!

542
00:24:28.842 --> 00:24:31.912
- I'll show you how it works.
- Sir, I don't know if this is necessary.

543
00:24:32.054 --> 00:24:34.373
Oh, don't worry.
I won't test it on you.

544
00:24:34.515 --> 00:24:36.117
I'll do it on your parents!

545
00:24:37.393 --> 00:24:38.289
What?

546
00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:40.003
- Hi, son.
- Hi!

547
00:24:40.145 --> 00:24:41.747
How's it going in the big city?

548
00:24:41.897 --> 00:24:44.125
Mommy. Daddy. What
are you doing here?

549
00:24:44.274 --> 00:24:46.797
Okay, Pa. I just want
you to act naturally.

550
00:24:46.944 --> 00:24:49.092
- Like you're going about your day.
- Gotcha.

551
00:24:49.238 --> 00:24:50.806
Yeah. Keep your hand up like that.

552
00:24:50.948 --> 00:24:51.890
Ma, scoot...

553
00:24:52.032 --> 00:24:53.805
two steps in to the right.

554
00:24:53.951 --> 00:24:55.974
- Pa, whenever I talk to Ma...
- Uh-huh?

555
00:24:56.120 --> 00:24:57.495
- ...you start to move.
- Sorry, sir.

556
00:24:57.496 --> 00:24:58.768
Get back to where you were!

557
00:24:58.914 --> 00:24:59.731
- Here?
- Perfect.

558
00:24:59.873 --> 00:25:02.351
That's great. You can't do anything better.
No reason why you should move.

559
00:25:02.501 --> 00:25:03.102
Right.

560
00:25:03.252 --> 00:25:03.853
Now, Ma...

561
00:25:04.003 --> 00:25:05.605
hand on his shoulder. And you...

562
00:25:05.754 --> 00:25:08.198
- Pa, you just moved and you've just wrecked it!
- Uh-huh.

563
00:25:08.340 --> 00:25:09.111
You wrecked it!

564
00:25:09.258 --> 00:25:11.531
Bad Cop, you see what
I'm talking about?

565
00:25:11.677 --> 00:25:15.532
All I'm asking for
is total perfection.

566
00:25:15.681 --> 00:25:17.203
Send in a Micro-manager!

567
00:25:20.227 --> 00:25:21.499
Commencing micro-management.

568
00:25:24.690 --> 00:25:25.990
Hold still, you guys.

569
00:25:28.777 --> 00:25:29.673
And then...

570
00:25:29.820 --> 00:25:31.172
I just spray them...

571
00:25:31.321 --> 00:25:32.638
with the TAKOS.

572
00:25:34.158 --> 00:25:35.555
Oh, Pa, hold me.

573
00:25:35.701 --> 00:25:38.896
Oh, darling, I can't move me legs.

574
00:25:39.038 --> 00:25:41.140
- Does that upset you, Bad Cop?
- Um...

575
00:25:41.290 --> 00:25:44.644
Surely you feel bad for your parents,
and you wanna help them, don't you?

576
00:25:44.793 --> 00:25:48.693
We're okay, son.
Just a little stuck, is all.

577
00:25:48.839 --> 00:25:50.532
Go ahead...

578
00:25:52.092 --> 00:25:53.785
finish the job.

579
00:25:53.927 --> 00:25:55.324
Of course, sir.

580
00:25:55.471 --> 00:25:56.663
No, I don't want to.

581
00:25:56.805 --> 00:25:58.407
- You have to.
- I don't want to.

582
00:25:58.557 --> 00:26:00.177
- Would you please be quiet?
- I can't.

583
00:26:00.309 --> 00:26:01.684
- You must. Shut it!
- But they...

584
00:26:01.685 --> 00:26:03.753
- It's not nice.
- It's your job, man.

585
00:26:03.896 --> 00:26:05.122
I can't do it.

586
00:26:05.272 --> 00:26:06.965
- They're innocent.
- Just as I thought.

587
00:26:07.107 --> 00:26:09.960
Your Good Cop side's
making you soft, Bad Cop.

588
00:26:10.110 --> 00:26:10.881
Robots!

589
00:26:11.028 --> 00:26:13.506
Bring me the fleece-crested
Scepter of Q-Teep...

590
00:26:13.655 --> 00:26:15.678
and the Po-Lish Remover of Na-ll.

591
00:26:15.824 --> 00:26:18.177
You've already let The
Special get away once.

592
00:26:18.327 --> 00:26:19.019
Sir.

593
00:26:19.161 --> 00:26:21.309
I'm just gonna make sure
it doesn't happen again.

594
00:26:21.455 --> 00:26:23.728
No more Mr. Nice Guy!

595
00:26:28.921 --> 00:26:29.988
Oh, son!

596
00:26:30.130 --> 00:26:33.951
On Taco Tuesday, I'm going to
Kragleize the entire universe...

597
00:26:34.093 --> 00:26:37.242
so that everyone will stop
messing with my stuff!

598
00:26:37.387 --> 00:26:39.114
Are you gonna be with me...

599
00:26:39.264 --> 00:26:40.832
or are you gonna be stuck...

600
00:26:40.974 --> 00:26:43.998
having a tea party
with your mom and dad?

601
00:26:44.144 --> 00:26:45.040
SOon?

602
00:26:46.355 --> 00:26:47.377
Sorry, Dad.

603
00:26:48.816 --> 00:26:50.418
I have a job to do.

604
00:27:08.127 --> 00:27:10.487
All you have to do is blend in
and act like you belong here.

605
00:27:10.546 --> 00:27:11.647
Ah, perfect.

606
00:27:11.797 --> 00:27:14.275
Well, hi there, I'm a cowboy!

607
00:27:14.424 --> 00:27:15.804
Bang, bang, bang-bang-bang-bang!

608
00:27:16.385 --> 00:27:17.737
Shoot, shoot, shoot.
Bullet, bullet, gun.

609
00:27:17.886 --> 00:27:20.034
Zap, zap, zap, pow. Zap, pow.

610
00:27:20.180 --> 00:27:22.374
- What are they looking at?
- I made a mistake.

611
00:27:22.516 --> 00:27:24.038
You should just be still.
Act like a stool.

612
00:27:24.184 --> 00:27:25.456
- Wait!
- Howdy, guys!

613
00:27:25.602 --> 00:27:27.702
- Quiet. Nope, stools don't talk.
- Come sit on me.

614
00:27:27.771 --> 00:27:29.123
Okay, shh.

615
00:27:29.273 --> 00:27:30.875
Let me show you how it's done.

616
00:27:36.113 --> 00:27:37.180
What a lady!

617
00:27:38.699 --> 00:27:41.268
Okay, let me just
find the wizard...

618
00:27:41.410 --> 00:27:43.308
and get this over with.

619
00:27:48.959 --> 00:27:50.777
- Ooh!
- There he is.

620
00:27:51.128 --> 00:27:52.821
- Vitruvius.
- Who?

621
00:27:52.963 --> 00:27:55.566
I've never heard of that
man, whom I am not.

622
00:27:55.716 --> 00:27:57.443
- Who are you?
- It's me.

623
00:27:57.676 --> 00:28:00.279
I am a blind man and cannot see.

624
00:28:00.429 --> 00:28:01.530
- It's Wyldstyle.
- Oof.

625
00:28:01.680 --> 00:28:02.747
Are you a DJ?

626
00:28:02.890 --> 00:28:04.870
- What? Why does everybody...?
- Oh, wait, wait.

627
00:28:04.933 --> 00:28:06.513
Are you the student
I used to have...

628
00:28:06.560 --> 00:28:08.501
who was so insecure she
kept changing her name?

629
00:28:08.520 --> 00:28:09.212
No, no, no.

630
00:28:09.354 --> 00:28:10.831
- First Darkstorm, then Geminizzle.
- No. Never.

631
00:28:10.981 --> 00:28:13.041
Then Neversmile, then Freakface,
then Snazzypants.

632
00:28:13.150 --> 00:28:14.172
Okay. All right, yes.

633
00:28:14.318 --> 00:28:16.295
Meet me upstairs in 10 seconds.

634
00:28:25.037 --> 00:28:26.889
Oh, man.

635
00:28:27.664 --> 00:28:29.186
You have a very weirdly...

636
00:28:29.333 --> 00:28:31.060
- ...decorated place.
- Thank you.

637
00:28:31.210 --> 00:28:34.484
Vitruvius, we have found
the Piece of Resistance.

638
00:28:34.630 --> 00:28:36.323
- Is it true?
- Yes, but...

639
00:28:36.465 --> 00:28:38.693
Wyldstyle.
The prophecy states that...

640
00:28:38.842 --> 00:28:40.615
you are The Special.

641
00:28:40.761 --> 00:28:43.239
The embodiment of
good, foiler of evil.

642
00:28:43.388 --> 00:28:45.411
The most talented,
most brilliant...

643
00:28:45.557 --> 00:28:48.501
most important person
in the universe.

644
00:28:48.644 --> 00:28:50.997
That would be great...

645
00:28:51.605 --> 00:28:53.425
but Emmet is the one
who found the Piece.

646
00:28:54.399 --> 00:28:55.500
Oh, okay. Emmet!

647
00:28:55.651 --> 00:28:56.968
The prophecy states that...

648
00:28:57.110 --> 00:28:58.837
you are The Special.

649
00:28:58.987 --> 00:29:01.556
- The most talented...
- I'm not sure he's The Special.

650
00:29:01.698 --> 00:29:03.300
Because he's not even a
MasterBuilder. Watch.

651
00:29:03.450 --> 00:29:05.070
Emmet, just given
what's around you...

652
00:29:05.202 --> 00:29:06.224
- ...build something simple.
- Okay.

653
00:29:06.370 --> 00:29:07.392
- Like an awesome race car.
- Great.

654
00:29:07.537 --> 00:29:09.139
- Go.
- Do you have the instructions?

655
00:29:09.289 --> 00:29:12.814
No. You must create the instructions
in your mind, my liege.

656
00:29:12.960 --> 00:29:15.404
Ah. Okay. Race car.

657
00:29:15.545 --> 00:29:16.567
Um...

658
00:29:16.713 --> 00:29:19.407
Well, there's a lot of
really cool stuff here.

659
00:29:19.549 --> 00:29:22.528
Don't see a wheel...

660
00:29:22.678 --> 00:29:24.451
or...

661
00:29:28.475 --> 00:29:30.077
three more wheels.

662
00:29:30.227 --> 00:29:33.046
See? He can't do it. He will
never be a MasterBuilder.

663
00:29:33.188 --> 00:29:35.586
Of course not. Not if you
keep telling him he can't.

664
00:29:35.732 --> 00:29:37.334
He needs to see that he can.

665
00:29:37.484 --> 00:29:38.506
What are you doing?

666
00:29:38.652 --> 00:29:40.593
- We are entering your mind...
- What?

667
00:29:40.696 --> 00:29:42.844
to prove that you have the
unlocked potential...

668
00:29:42.990 --> 00:29:44.512
to be a MasterBuilder.

669
00:29:44.658 --> 00:29:45.975
Ujjayi breath.

670
00:29:52.124 --> 00:29:54.025
Whoa, are we inside
my brain right now?

671
00:29:54.167 --> 00:29:56.941
- It's big. I must be smart.
- Mm-hm.

672
00:29:57.087 --> 00:29:59.861
I'm not hearing a lot
of activity here.

673
00:30:00.007 --> 00:30:02.610
I don't think he's ever had an
original thought. In his life.

674
00:30:02.759 --> 00:30:03.826
Ha, ha. That's not true.

675
00:30:03.969 --> 00:30:05.912
For instance, one time
I wanted to have...

676
00:30:06.054 --> 00:30:08.122
a bunch of my friends
over to watch TV...

677
00:30:08.265 --> 00:30:11.790
Not unlike this TV that
just showed up magically.

678
00:30:11.935 --> 00:30:13.878
And not everybody can
fit on my one couch...

679
00:30:14.021 --> 00:30:15.202
and I thought to myself:

680
00:30:15.314 --> 00:30:17.294
"What if there was such a
thing as a bunk bed...

681
00:30:17.316 --> 00:30:18.542
but as a couch?"

682
00:30:18.692 --> 00:30:21.090
Introducing the
double-decker couch.

683
00:30:21.236 --> 00:30:24.180
So everyone could watch TV
together and be buddies!

684
00:30:24.948 --> 00:30:27.088
That is literally the dumbest
thing I've ever heard.

685
00:30:27.200 --> 00:30:29.644
Please, Wyldstyle,
let me handle this.

686
00:30:29.786 --> 00:30:32.730
That idea is just the worst.

687
00:30:32.873 --> 00:30:34.691
There must be something
around here...

688
00:30:34.833 --> 00:30:36.105
that proves his potential.

689
00:30:36.251 --> 00:30:38.774
If The Man Upstairs chose
him to be The Special...

690
00:30:38.920 --> 00:30:40.146
there must be a reason.

691
00:30:40.297 --> 00:30:41.797
- Who's The Man Upstairs?
- See?

692
00:30:41.798 --> 00:30:43.549
He doesn't even know
about The Man Upstairs.

693
00:30:43.550 --> 00:30:45.111
Does he have, like,
super-gross hands...

694
00:30:45.177 --> 00:30:47.386
that look like they're made
out of big pink sausages?

695
00:30:47.387 --> 00:30:49.489
Like eagle talons mixed with squid?

696
00:30:49.639 --> 00:30:52.288
Wait. You've seen the...?

697
00:30:53.060 --> 00:30:53.752
Whoa!

698
00:30:53.894 --> 00:30:55.837
That's what I was
just thinking about.

699
00:30:55.979 --> 00:30:56.750
How did you...?

700
00:30:56.897 --> 00:30:58.123
I had this weird dream
when I touched the Piece.

701
00:30:58.273 --> 00:31:00.375
Well, I mean, I wasn't asleep,
so it wasn't really a dream.

702
00:31:00.525 --> 00:31:02.673
Emmet, you had a vision.

703
00:31:02.819 --> 00:31:03.715
I did?

704
00:31:03.862 --> 00:31:05.430
MasterBuilders spend years...

705
00:31:05.572 --> 00:31:07.615
training themselves to clear
their minds enough...

706
00:31:07.616 --> 00:31:10.970
to have even a fleeting glimpse
of The Man Upstairs...

707
00:31:11.119 --> 00:31:14.894
and yet, your mind is already
so prodigiously empty...

708
00:31:15.040 --> 00:31:18.144
that there is nothing in it to
clear away in the first place.

709
00:31:18.293 --> 00:31:19.485
With proper training...

710
00:31:19.669 --> 00:31:22.147
you could become a
great MasterBuilder.

711
00:31:22.297 --> 00:31:23.319
I could?

712
00:31:23.465 --> 00:31:25.818
The prophecy chose you, Emmet.

713
00:31:26.301 --> 00:31:28.028
But I can't do any of the stuff...

714
00:31:28.178 --> 00:31:30.038
that the prophecy says
I'm supposed to do.

715
00:31:30.180 --> 00:31:33.875
All you have to do is to believe.

716
00:31:34.059 --> 00:31:34.785
Then...

717
00:31:35.519 --> 00:31:37.713
you will see everything.

718
00:31:38.480 --> 00:31:39.957
Are you ready, my son?

719
00:31:42.984 --> 00:31:44.757
Yes, I am.

720
00:31:45.487 --> 00:31:46.839
I think.

721
00:31:46.988 --> 00:31:48.886
Then we haven't a moment to lose.

722
00:31:49.032 --> 00:31:50.600
We must assemble...

723
00:31:51.159 --> 00:31:52.602
the MasterBuilders.

724
00:31:53.120 --> 00:31:55.268
Do you think Zeppelins
are a bad investment?

725
00:32:07.717 --> 00:32:09.945
Any of you fellas seen this guy?

726
00:32:12.597 --> 00:32:13.937
Wait a minute, partner.

727
00:32:14.057 --> 00:32:15.830
Draw a cowboy hat on him.

728
00:32:22.441 --> 00:32:24.464
These mechanical birds
will get our message out.

729
00:32:24.609 --> 00:32:26.211
They will go to an Internet café...

730
00:32:26.361 --> 00:32:28.112
and e-mail the remaining
MasterBuilders...

731
00:32:28.113 --> 00:32:31.262
who will meet us in the secret
realm of Cloud Cuckooland.

732
00:32:31.408 --> 00:32:34.102
Cuckooland? Wait. What happened
to that whole training part?

733
00:32:34.244 --> 00:32:35.937
Don't worry, Emmet.

734
00:32:36.079 --> 00:32:37.852
Your training begins now.

735
00:32:39.249 --> 00:32:40.150
Piano man...

736
00:32:40.292 --> 00:32:41.143
open up.

737
00:32:41.293 --> 00:32:42.861
Your training begins later!

738
00:32:45.005 --> 00:32:46.072
On three.

739
00:32:46.214 --> 00:32:47.065
One...

740
00:32:53.805 --> 00:32:56.499
- Whew. I think we're in the clear.
- Freeze, turkeys.

741
00:32:57.809 --> 00:32:59.456
All I want is the
Piece of Resistance.

742
00:32:59.603 --> 00:33:01.797
We would rather he died
than give it to you.

743
00:33:01.938 --> 00:33:04.336
I would not rather he died.

744
00:33:04.483 --> 00:33:07.507
Look, everybody, we can do this
the easy way, or we can do it...

745
00:33:07.652 --> 00:33:08.472
Go, run!

746
00:33:08.570 --> 00:33:10.047
They took the hard way. Fire!

747
00:33:10.197 --> 00:33:11.298
Fire!

748
00:33:12.199 --> 00:33:14.339
Vitruvius, which way
to Cloud Cuckooland?

749
00:33:14.409 --> 00:33:16.452
Head for the big bright
thing in the sky.

750
00:33:16.453 --> 00:33:18.396
- You mean the sun?
- Yeah. Yeah, that's it.

751
00:33:18.538 --> 00:33:19.810
Let's get out of here.
Here, use this.

752
00:33:19.956 --> 00:33:21.016
What? Wait, hey...

753
00:33:21.124 --> 00:33:23.065
- What are you doing? Aah!
- Let's go!

754
00:33:24.294 --> 00:33:26.146
I don't know what I'm doing.

755
00:33:29.382 --> 00:33:30.404
Goodbye.

756
00:33:30.550 --> 00:33:31.776
Boom!

757
00:33:38.099 --> 00:33:39.371
Oh, dang!

758
00:33:43.063 --> 00:33:45.461
Aah! I've got pigs! I hate pigs!

759
00:33:45.607 --> 00:33:47.380
Quit playing around in the mud.
I could use your help.

760
00:33:47.526 --> 00:33:49.503
Wyldstyle, we could really use...

761
00:33:49.653 --> 00:33:50.345
your help!

762
00:33:50.487 --> 00:33:51.554
Oink, oink, oink.

763
00:34:08.547 --> 00:34:09.694
Oink!

764
00:34:10.715 --> 00:34:12.675
Vitruvius, they're gaining
on us. Build something!

765
00:34:12.759 --> 00:34:13.826
Let Emmet try!

766
00:34:13.969 --> 00:34:16.618
No, let's not let Emmet try!
I haven't had any training.

767
00:34:16.763 --> 00:34:17.455
That's okay.

768
00:34:17.597 --> 00:34:19.699
We'll start with how to
become a MasterBuilder.

769
00:34:19.849 --> 00:34:22.498
Step one: Trust your instincts.

770
00:34:22.644 --> 00:34:23.540
Okay, okay. Um...

771
00:34:23.687 --> 00:34:25.209
Build something! Build something!

772
00:34:25.355 --> 00:34:26.627
Aha. Take that!

773
00:34:30.944 --> 00:34:33.672
Unless your instincts are terrible.

774
00:34:39.869 --> 00:34:40.845
No! The wheel!

775
00:34:46.084 --> 00:34:48.403
I can't control it much longer!

776
00:34:48.545 --> 00:34:51.740
Emmet, we need to attach the wheel
to something that spins around.

777
00:34:51.881 --> 00:34:52.573
Um...

778
00:34:52.716 --> 00:34:54.818
<i>We need to attach the wheel to
something that spins around.</i>

779
00:34:54.968 --> 00:34:56.866
<i>We need to attach the wheel to
something that spins around.</i>

780
00:34:57.012 --> 00:34:59.615
<i>We need to attach the wheel to
something that spins around.</i>

781
00:34:59.764 --> 00:35:02.708
<i>Something that spins around.
Spins around. Spins around.</i>

782
00:35:03.143 --> 00:35:04.415
Oh.

783
00:35:05.645 --> 00:35:07.747
Emmet, where are you going?

784
00:35:10.358 --> 00:35:11.380
Oh, this better work.

785
00:35:11.526 --> 00:35:12.923
Hang tight!

786
00:35:14.070 --> 00:35:16.639
Dagnabit!

787
00:35:18.533 --> 00:35:19.805
Well done, Emmet.

788
00:35:20.577 --> 00:35:21.769
Hey! I did it.

789
00:35:21.911 --> 00:35:24.105
Wow. You actually did it.

790
00:35:26.499 --> 00:35:27.316
Train!

791
00:35:34.841 --> 00:35:36.158
Oh, no.

792
00:35:36.301 --> 00:35:37.948
Get off my train.

793
00:35:38.094 --> 00:35:39.161
Run!

794
00:35:44.434 --> 00:35:45.330
Wyldstyle!

795
00:35:48.313 --> 00:35:49.790
Owie!

796
00:35:49.939 --> 00:35:51.165
He's gonna ram us.

797
00:35:51.650 --> 00:35:53.468
Quick, quick, quick! That piece!
Give me that piece.

798
00:35:53.610 --> 00:35:54.962
Huh?

799
00:35:55.111 --> 00:35:56.713
Build a ramp!

800
00:36:02.869 --> 00:36:04.016
What the heck?

801
00:36:04.204 --> 00:36:05.851
Rest in pieces.

802
00:36:07.832 --> 00:36:08.774
- Uh...
- Oh, no.

803
00:36:08.917 --> 00:36:09.984
Wait. No, no, no.

804
00:36:18.218 --> 00:36:19.365
Hey.

805
00:36:19.761 --> 00:36:21.659
Thanks for saving
my life back there.

806
00:36:21.805 --> 00:36:23.282
Even if, you know...

807
00:36:23.431 --> 00:36:26.660
eventually it turned
out to be pointless.

808
00:36:27.268 --> 00:36:29.621
Well, for what it's worth...

809
00:36:29.771 --> 00:36:32.966
this has been about the
greatest 15 minutes of my life.

810
00:36:39.781 --> 00:36:40.473
What the...?

811
00:36:43.743 --> 00:36:45.345
Relax, everybody, I'm here.

812
00:36:45.495 --> 00:36:46.221
Batman!

813
00:36:46.371 --> 00:36:47.746
- What's up, babe?
- Babe!

814
00:36:47.747 --> 00:36:49.645
- What?
- Oh, sorry. Batman, this is Emmet.

815
00:36:49.791 --> 00:36:51.985
Emmet, this is my
boyfriend, Batman.

816
00:36:52.127 --> 00:36:53.695
I'm Batman.

817
00:36:53.837 --> 00:36:56.656
That's your boyfriend? Aah!

818
00:36:58.550 --> 00:37:00.323
Batman, huh? Where'd you guys meet?

819
00:37:00.468 --> 00:37:02.946
It's actually a funny
story, right, Bat?

820
00:37:03.096 --> 00:37:04.163
There he is.

821
00:37:04.305 --> 00:37:06.499
- "Police" to meet you, Bad Cop.
- Batman!

822
00:37:06.641 --> 00:37:07.412
The pleasure...

823
00:37:07.559 --> 00:37:08.455
is all "spine."

824
00:37:08.601 --> 00:37:09.748
Guess what...

825
00:37:09.894 --> 00:37:10.836
you big dumb baby.

826
00:37:10.979 --> 00:37:13.423
Your car is a baby carriage.

827
00:37:14.774 --> 00:37:16.342
Oh, no, your boyfriend's gone.

828
00:37:16.484 --> 00:37:17.631
- Hey, babe.
- What?

829
00:37:17.777 --> 00:37:18.878
Let's hold hands.

830
00:37:21.740 --> 00:37:23.183
So, uh...

831
00:37:23.324 --> 00:37:25.677
Hey, guys, I think we're
about to crash into the sun.

832
00:37:25.827 --> 00:37:28.021
Yeah, but it's gonna
look really cool.

833
00:37:33.960 --> 00:37:36.734
Uh, is this Cloud Cuckooland?
I don't see any clouds.

834
00:37:36.880 --> 00:37:38.698
- Or cuckoos.
- No, no, this is...

835
00:37:38.840 --> 00:37:39.736
Middle Zealand.

836
00:37:39.883 --> 00:37:41.280
A wondrous land...

837
00:37:41.426 --> 00:37:43.046
<i>full of knights, castles, mutton...</i>

838
00:37:43.094 --> 00:37:45.447
<i>torture weapons, poverty,
leeches, illiteracy...</i>

839
00:37:45.597 --> 00:37:47.074
and, um...

840
00:37:47.223 --> 00:37:48.370
Dragon!

841
00:37:49.350 --> 00:37:51.202
Yeah, that too.

842
00:37:53.897 --> 00:37:56.466
Once we arrive at Cloud Cuckooland,
we'll raise an army...

843
00:37:56.608 --> 00:37:57.379
of MasterBuilders to...

844
00:37:57.525 --> 00:38:00.754
Anyway, you guys gotta check out
these new subwoofers I installed.

845
00:38:00.904 --> 00:38:03.006
I call them the dogs.
Listen to them bark!

846
00:38:04.824 --> 00:38:05.925
Can you turn that
down a little bit?

847
00:38:06.075 --> 00:38:08.769
This is a song I
wrote for Wyldstyle.

848
00:38:08.912 --> 00:38:10.389
<i>Darkness</i>

849
00:38:10.538 --> 00:38:12.060
It's about how I'm an orphan.

850
00:38:12.207 --> 00:38:13.809
<i>No parents</i>

851
00:38:13.958 --> 00:38:15.560
This is real music, Emmet.

852
00:38:15.710 --> 00:38:18.438
Batman's a true artist.
Dark, brooding.

853
00:38:18.588 --> 00:38:20.656
Well, I'm dark and brooding too.

854
00:38:20.799 --> 00:38:22.776
Guys, look, a rainbow.

855
00:38:22.926 --> 00:38:24.606
So you're gonna drive
up the curved part...

856
00:38:24.719 --> 00:38:25.536
<i>Super rich</i>

857
00:38:25.678 --> 00:38:27.137
take it all the way to the top...

858
00:38:27.138 --> 00:38:28.706
<i>Kind of makes it better</i>

859
00:38:28.848 --> 00:38:30.200
and park the car.

860
00:38:30.350 --> 00:38:34.250
Friends, welcome to Cloud
Cuckooland. Now...

861
00:38:37.440 --> 00:38:39.918
I just need to give
the secret knock.

862
00:38:51.287 --> 00:38:52.980
Okay.

863
00:39:00.129 --> 00:39:01.151
I'm just gonna come right out.

864
00:39:01.297 --> 00:39:04.196
I have no idea what's going on,
or what this place is at all.

865
00:39:04.342 --> 00:39:07.662
Hi! I am Princess Unikitty...

866
00:39:07.804 --> 00:39:11.158
and I welcome you all
to Cloud Cuckooland.

867
00:39:13.476 --> 00:39:15.704
There's no signs or anything.

868
00:39:15.854 --> 00:39:17.877
How does anyone know
what not to do?

869
00:39:18.022 --> 00:39:19.339
Here in Cloud Cuckooland...

870
00:39:19.482 --> 00:39:20.674
there are no rules.

871
00:39:20.817 --> 00:39:22.294
There's no government...

872
00:39:22.485 --> 00:39:23.882
no babysitters...

873
00:39:24.028 --> 00:39:25.300
no bedtimes...

874
00:39:25.446 --> 00:39:27.093
no frowny faces...

875
00:39:27.282 --> 00:39:29.180
no bushy mustaches...

876
00:39:29.325 --> 00:39:31.644
and no negativity of any kind.

877
00:39:31.786 --> 00:39:33.846
You just said the word "no"
like a thousand times.

878
00:39:33.913 --> 00:39:36.266
And there's also no consistency.

879
00:39:36.457 --> 00:39:38.309
I hate this place.

880
00:39:38.459 --> 00:39:40.436
Any idea is a good idea...

881
00:39:40.587 --> 00:39:42.314
except the not happy ones.

882
00:39:42.463 --> 00:39:44.440
Those you push down deep inside...

883
00:39:44.591 --> 00:39:46.910
where you'll never, ever, ever...

884
00:39:47.051 --> 00:39:47.743
ever...

885
00:39:47.886 --> 00:39:49.704
find them.

886
00:39:49.846 --> 00:39:52.324
Your fellow MasterBuilders
are gathered in the Dog.

887
00:39:52.473 --> 00:39:53.699
The what?

888
00:39:56.394 --> 00:39:57.996
Ah! Is that Superman?

889
00:39:59.230 --> 00:40:00.001
Girl, what are you doing?

890
00:40:00.148 --> 00:40:02.091
- Hey, Superman!
- Oh, hey. What's up?

891
00:40:02.233 --> 00:40:04.176
- Lantern. Green Lantern.
- Yeah, yeah.

892
00:40:04.319 --> 00:40:05.921
You wanna sit together
at the meeting?

893
00:40:06.070 --> 00:40:08.719
Um, I have to go back to Krypton.

894
00:40:08.865 --> 00:40:10.012
Didn't Krypton blow up?

895
00:40:10.158 --> 00:40:13.432
My fellow MasterBuilders,
including but not limited to...

896
00:40:13.578 --> 00:40:14.828
Robin Hood, Mermaid Lady...

897
00:40:14.829 --> 00:40:15.449
Gandalf...

898
00:40:15.580 --> 00:40:16.330
Swamp Creature...

899
00:40:16.331 --> 00:40:18.183
- ...1980-something Space Guy...
- Hello!

900
00:40:18.333 --> 00:40:20.276
2002 NBA All-Stars...

901
00:40:20.418 --> 00:40:22.111
- ...and Wonder Woman.
- Unh!

902
00:40:22.253 --> 00:40:25.653
You have traveled far to be here
for a moment of great import.

903
00:40:25.798 --> 00:40:26.820
We have learned...

904
00:40:26.966 --> 00:40:28.989
that Lord Business
plans to unleash...

905
00:40:29.135 --> 00:40:30.828
a fully weaponized Kragle...

906
00:40:30.970 --> 00:40:32.538
on Taco Tuesday...

907
00:40:32.680 --> 00:40:35.158
to end the world as we know it.

908
00:40:36.309 --> 00:40:37.535
Please, calm yourselves.

909
00:40:37.685 --> 00:40:38.346
Green Ninja...

910
00:40:38.436 --> 00:40:39.097
Milhouse...

911
00:40:39.187 --> 00:40:40.007
Nice Vampire...

912
00:40:40.146 --> 00:40:41.526
Michelangelo, Michelangelo...

913
00:40:41.648 --> 00:40:42.749
and Cleopatra.

914
00:40:42.899 --> 00:40:44.717
There is yet one hope.

915
00:40:44.859 --> 00:40:46.836
The Special has arisen.

916
00:40:48.571 --> 00:40:50.344
Have the young man step forward.

917
00:40:50.490 --> 00:40:51.591
As you wish, Dubbledore.

918
00:40:51.741 --> 00:40:52.558
I'm Gandalf!

919
00:40:52.700 --> 00:40:54.848
- It's pronounced "Dumbledore."
- Dubbadore?

920
00:40:54.994 --> 00:40:56.346
No, "Dumbledore."

921
00:40:56.496 --> 00:40:57.313
Thought you said "Dubbadore."

922
00:40:57.455 --> 00:40:58.147
Vitruvius!

923
00:40:58.289 --> 00:41:00.749
You gotta write that down. I'm
not gonna remember any of it.

924
00:41:00.750 --> 00:41:02.067
But here we go.

925
00:41:03.586 --> 00:41:07.281
The Special will now
give an eloquent speech.

926
00:41:11.469 --> 00:41:13.162
Go ahead, man. You got this.

927
00:41:14.847 --> 00:41:15.948
Okay.

928
00:41:22.271 --> 00:41:24.624
Hello. I'm Emmet.

929
00:41:24.983 --> 00:41:27.006
Oh, and this is the
Piece of Resistance.

930
00:41:36.411 --> 00:41:37.683
Thank you.

931
00:41:38.121 --> 00:41:41.020
Well, uh, I know that I, for one...

932
00:41:41.165 --> 00:41:43.518
am very excited to
work with you guys...

933
00:41:43.668 --> 00:41:45.691
to get into the Octan
Tower, find the Kragle...

934
00:41:45.837 --> 00:41:47.939
and put this thing on the thing.

935
00:41:48.089 --> 00:41:50.692
And I know it's going to
be really hard, but...

936
00:41:50.842 --> 00:41:52.194
"Really hard"?

937
00:41:53.469 --> 00:41:56.914
Wiping ye bum with a hook
for a hand is really hard.

938
00:41:57.056 --> 00:41:58.829
This be impossible.

939
00:41:58.975 --> 00:42:01.919
The last time we tried to storm
Lord Business' office...

940
00:42:02.061 --> 00:42:04.334
we used every plan
we could conceive.

941
00:42:04.480 --> 00:42:07.834
The result was a massacre
too terrible to speak of.

942
00:42:08.317 --> 00:42:09.213
Who are you?

943
00:42:09.360 --> 00:42:11.554
The name be Metal Beard.

944
00:42:11.696 --> 00:42:14.299
And I'll tell you me tale of woe.

945
00:42:14.449 --> 00:42:16.176
Oh, great, here we go again.

946
00:42:16.325 --> 00:42:17.051
I arrived...

947
00:42:17.201 --> 00:42:18.501
<i>at the foot of the Tower...</i>

948
00:42:18.619 --> 00:42:21.393
<i>with me hearty
MasterBuilder crew...</i>

949
00:42:21.539 --> 00:42:25.644
<i>only to find the Kragle was all the
way up on the infinityeth floor...</i>

950
00:42:25.793 --> 00:42:28.237
<i>guarded by a robot army...</i>

951
00:42:28.379 --> 00:42:29.560
<i>and security measures...</i>

952
00:42:29.589 --> 00:42:30.906
<i>of every kind...</i>

953
00:42:31.049 --> 00:42:32.275
<i>imaginable:</i>

954
00:42:32.425 --> 00:42:33.572
<i>Lasers...</i>

955
00:42:34.218 --> 00:42:35.661
<i>sharks...</i>

956
00:42:35.970 --> 00:42:37.868
<i>laser sharks...</i>

957
00:42:38.014 --> 00:42:39.616
<i>overbearing assistants...</i>

958
00:42:40.850 --> 00:42:42.952
<i>and strange, dangerous relics...</i>

959
00:42:43.102 --> 00:42:43.998
<i>that entrap...</i>

960
00:42:44.145 --> 00:42:44.837
<i>snap...</i>

961
00:42:44.979 --> 00:42:46.046
<i>and zap.</i>

962
00:42:46.189 --> 00:42:50.214
And there be a mysterious
room called the Think Tank.

963
00:42:51.152 --> 00:42:52.674
<i>I barely made it out of that...</i>

964
00:42:52.820 --> 00:42:53.546
<i>room...</i>

965
00:42:53.696 --> 00:42:54.672
<i>with just me head!</i>

966
00:42:56.616 --> 00:42:58.844
<i>And organs.</i>

967
00:42:58.993 --> 00:42:59.764
Okay.

968
00:42:59.911 --> 00:43:02.764
I had to replace every part
of my once-strapping...

969
00:43:02.914 --> 00:43:04.436
virile pirate body...

970
00:43:04.582 --> 00:43:08.232
with this useless hunk of
garbage ye see before ye.

971
00:43:08.377 --> 00:43:12.107
So if ye think it'd be a
good idea to return...

972
00:43:12.256 --> 00:43:13.477
to that forsaken place...

973
00:43:13.549 --> 00:43:14.741
Special...

974
00:43:14.884 --> 00:43:17.032
what idea have ye that be better...

975
00:43:17.178 --> 00:43:18.825
than the ideas of 100...

976
00:43:18.971 --> 00:43:21.540
of our fallen
MasterBuilder brothers?

977
00:43:21.974 --> 00:43:23.417
Well, uh...

978
00:43:23.559 --> 00:43:26.538
Well, technically I'm not
exactly a MasterBuilder yet.

979
00:43:26.687 --> 00:43:27.709
What?

980
00:43:29.023 --> 00:43:31.717
Please! Everyone! Please!

981
00:43:32.276 --> 00:43:33.377
Rubbish!

982
00:43:33.528 --> 00:43:35.255
Yes, it's true.

983
00:43:35.404 --> 00:43:38.178
I may not be a MasterBuilder.

984
00:43:38.324 --> 00:43:40.347
I may not have a lot
of experience...

985
00:43:40.493 --> 00:43:43.722
fighting or leading or
coming up with plans.

986
00:43:44.205 --> 00:43:46.273
Or having ideas in general.

987
00:43:46.999 --> 00:43:50.069
In fact, I'm not all that smart.

988
00:43:50.211 --> 00:43:53.941
And I'm not what you'd
call a "creative type."

989
00:43:54.382 --> 00:43:55.654
Plus...

990
00:43:55.800 --> 00:43:57.994
generally unskilled.

991
00:43:58.886 --> 00:44:00.033
Also...

992
00:44:00.179 --> 00:44:02.953
scared and cowardly.

993
00:44:03.975 --> 00:44:05.497
I know what you're thinking:

994
00:44:05.977 --> 00:44:08.125
"He is the least
qualified person...

995
00:44:08.271 --> 00:44:10.590
in the world to lead us."

996
00:44:11.524 --> 00:44:13.001
And you are right.

997
00:44:13.151 --> 00:44:16.221
This is supposed to
make us feel better?

998
00:44:16.362 --> 00:44:18.635
No, there was about to be a "but."

999
00:44:18.781 --> 00:44:20.724
- You're a butt!
- Yes.

1000
00:44:20.867 --> 00:44:23.186
You all be on your own!

1001
00:44:23.327 --> 00:44:25.930
I be leaving this lost cause!

1002
00:44:28.082 --> 00:44:29.183
Why are you leaving?

1003
00:44:29.333 --> 00:44:32.357
A house divided against
itself would be better...

1004
00:44:32.503 --> 00:44:33.695
than this.

1005
00:44:33.838 --> 00:44:35.235
Abraham Lincoln!

1006
00:44:35.381 --> 00:44:37.404
You bring your space
chair right back here!

1007
00:44:37.550 --> 00:44:39.277
Come on, guys!

1008
00:44:39.427 --> 00:44:42.246
We can still do this. Right?

1009
00:44:42.388 --> 00:44:44.115
You're not even a bit special.

1010
00:44:44.265 --> 00:44:46.914
Well, you were right about
him being a ding-dong.

1011
00:44:47.059 --> 00:44:48.752
You're a huge disappointment.

1012
00:44:49.395 --> 00:44:52.214
Get him out of here.
I don't wanna look at him.

1013
00:44:55.693 --> 00:44:58.012
Well, at least it
can't get any worse.

1014
00:45:00.114 --> 00:45:01.386
I was wrong.

1015
00:45:04.869 --> 00:45:06.391
It's the Orb of Tee-ti-list!

1016
00:45:07.455 --> 00:45:09.398
Ruh-roh. It's the bad guys.

1017
00:45:10.249 --> 00:45:11.441
Whoa. How did he...?

1018
00:45:11.584 --> 00:45:14.403
Go! Run! Come on, everyone!
Protect The Special.

1019
00:45:14.545 --> 00:45:16.022
What's that on his ankle?

1020
00:45:17.131 --> 00:45:18.824
It's a tracking device.

1021
00:45:20.051 --> 00:45:21.027
Take the MasterBuilders prisoner.

1022
00:45:21.177 --> 00:45:22.779
Oh, he led them right to us.

1023
00:45:22.929 --> 00:45:25.202
Guys, no, no, no.
It's not my fault.

1024
00:45:25.348 --> 00:45:28.543
You are the worst leader I've
ever seen. To the Batmobile!

1025
00:45:30.311 --> 00:45:31.037
Dang it.

1026
00:45:31.187 --> 00:45:32.288
To the invisible jet!

1027
00:45:34.106 --> 00:45:36.083
- Dang it!
- Every man for himself.

1028
00:45:36.234 --> 00:45:38.132
No, we must protect the Piece.

1029
00:45:38.277 --> 00:45:39.754
Shaq, do you know what time...

1030
00:45:39.904 --> 00:45:41.881
- ...it is?
- It's game time.

1031
00:45:44.951 --> 00:45:46.769
Y'all ready for this?

1032
00:45:48.621 --> 00:45:50.473
Oh, no! They were ready for that.

1033
00:45:50.623 --> 00:45:51.363
It didn't break!

1034
00:45:51.499 --> 00:45:53.351
Because it's Kragled. Machine gum!

1035
00:45:54.794 --> 00:45:55.816
Fire!

1036
00:45:55.962 --> 00:45:56.904
No!

1037
00:45:57.046 --> 00:45:58.739
Aah! I can't move!

1038
00:45:58.881 --> 00:45:59.839
Don't worry, Superman.

1039
00:45:59.840 --> 00:46:01.541
- I'll get you out of there.
- No! Don't!

1040
00:46:01.592 --> 00:46:05.617
Aah! Oh, my gosh. My hands are stuck.
My legs are stuck as well.

1041
00:46:05.763 --> 00:46:06.864
I super hate you.

1042
00:46:07.056 --> 00:46:10.456
- Ow! You're pulling my torso off.
- Babe...

1043
00:46:10.601 --> 00:46:11.726
help me get him out of here.

1044
00:46:11.727 --> 00:46:13.079
I said "every man for himself."

1045
00:46:13.271 --> 00:46:14.964
Hey, you gotta be there for me.

1046
00:46:18.901 --> 00:46:19.877
Fine!

1047
00:46:20.027 --> 00:46:21.629
Fine. Fine. Fine.

1048
00:46:21.779 --> 00:46:23.756
- I need you to have a better attitude.
- I have a great...

1049
00:46:23.906 --> 00:46:25.633
- ...attitude.
- Ouch.

1050
00:46:25.783 --> 00:46:27.510
The Special's in the
northwest quadrant.

1051
00:46:27.660 --> 00:46:29.012
We've got him cornered.

1052
00:46:30.037 --> 00:46:30.818
Ouch. Ouch. Ouch.

1053
00:46:30.955 --> 00:46:31.977
Where'd he go?

1054
00:46:36.711 --> 00:46:37.607
Oh, no!

1055
00:46:37.753 --> 00:46:39.605
They've hit our silly
cloud stabilizers!

1056
00:46:39.755 --> 00:46:41.698
Let's go! We need to
get Emmet out of here.

1057
00:46:41.841 --> 00:46:44.945
- Can't we build something?
- Hey! I'm Ben. But you can call me Benny.

1058
00:46:45.094 --> 00:46:46.434
I can build a spaceship. Watch.

1059
00:46:46.512 --> 00:46:48.831
<i>Spaceship, spaceship, spaceship
Spaceship, spaceship</i>

1060
00:46:48.973 --> 00:46:50.950
No! You can't.
The skies are surrounded.

1061
00:46:51.100 --> 00:46:53.248
That's okay. I didn't
really wanna build...

1062
00:46:53.394 --> 00:46:54.894
a spaceship anyway. That's cool.

1063
00:46:54.895 --> 00:46:56.556
Where can we go where
we can't be found?

1064
00:46:56.647 --> 00:46:58.267
Maybe we could go underwater?

1065
00:46:58.399 --> 00:47:00.126
What if we went underwater?

1066
00:47:00.276 --> 00:47:01.093
Great idea, babe!

1067
00:47:01.235 --> 00:47:03.015
Thank you, Batman.
Your ideas are the best.

1068
00:47:03.154 --> 00:47:04.094
But I just said that.

1069
00:47:04.113 --> 00:47:07.183
- We could build a submarine.
- A Bat-Submarine, patent pending.

1070
00:47:07.325 --> 00:47:08.176
With rainbows!

1071
00:47:08.326 --> 00:47:10.303
And dream catchers, in
case we take a nap.

1072
00:47:10.453 --> 00:47:11.896
Like an underwater spaceship!

1073
00:47:12.038 --> 00:47:13.705
But you can't build
all of them at once.

1074
00:47:13.706 --> 00:47:15.183
Ready? Break.

1075
00:47:15.333 --> 00:47:16.059
Okay.

1076
00:47:16.208 --> 00:47:19.403
These are the colors I need:
Blue razzleberry and sour apple!

1077
00:47:19.545 --> 00:47:21.488
If anybody has black parts,
I need them, okay?

1078
00:47:21.630 --> 00:47:22.856
I only work in black.

1079
00:47:23.007 --> 00:47:25.109
And sometimes, very,
very dark gray.

1080
00:47:25.259 --> 00:47:26.531
- Use the yellow bricks!
- Hey, guys, can I help?

1081
00:47:26.677 --> 00:47:28.779
- No! It has to be this way!
- No, I need that!

1082
00:47:28.929 --> 00:47:29.746
Where is he?

1083
00:47:29.889 --> 00:47:32.162
Anyone know what this
is, and do you need it?

1084
00:47:32.308 --> 00:47:34.225
I think we could use wings
and rocket boosters.

1085
00:47:34.226 --> 00:47:35.828
Ew. Get your retro space
stuff out of my area.

1086
00:47:35.978 --> 00:47:39.048
You guys, hey, just tell me exactly
what to do. And how to do it.

1087
00:47:39.190 --> 00:47:42.464
Emmet, don't worry about
what the others are doing.

1088
00:47:42.818 --> 00:47:46.593
You must embrace what
is special about you!

1089
00:47:55.289 --> 00:47:55.981
There he is!

1090
00:47:56.123 --> 00:47:58.191
All units, attack the sub!

1091
00:48:02.588 --> 00:48:03.985
Emmet, get in here!

1092
00:48:09.178 --> 00:48:11.656
Stop him! Stop him!
Don't let him...

1093
00:48:11.806 --> 00:48:12.873
get to the water!

1094
00:48:13.015 --> 00:48:14.255
Dive, dive, dive! Everybody in!

1095
00:48:14.308 --> 00:48:15.250
We're going under!

1096
00:48:32.993 --> 00:48:34.345
Oh, no.

1097
00:48:54.390 --> 00:48:55.912
My home.

1098
00:48:57.726 --> 00:48:59.578
It's gone.

1099
00:49:02.857 --> 00:49:05.676
I feel something inside.

1100
00:49:05.818 --> 00:49:07.920
It's like the opposite
of happiness.

1101
00:49:08.070 --> 00:49:11.674
I must stay positive.

1102
00:49:14.493 --> 00:49:15.469
Ah. Bubble gums.

1103
00:49:17.329 --> 00:49:18.271
Butterflies.

1104
00:49:23.002 --> 00:49:25.070
Cotton candy.

1105
00:49:25.838 --> 00:49:27.986
Gosh, I'm so sorry, Unikitty.

1106
00:49:29.800 --> 00:49:32.244
Do you want to sit down
and talk about it?

1107
00:49:32.845 --> 00:49:36.620
What the heck is that?

1108
00:49:36.765 --> 00:49:38.617
It's a double-decker couch.

1109
00:49:38.767 --> 00:49:40.518
Which seemed like a good
idea at the time...

1110
00:49:40.519 --> 00:49:43.964
but I now realize it's
not super helpful.

1111
00:49:44.356 --> 00:49:46.754
But, you know, it has cup holders.

1112
00:49:46.901 --> 00:49:49.550
Seats flip up with
coolers underneath.

1113
00:49:50.779 --> 00:49:53.678
You are so disappointing
on so many levels.

1114
00:49:53.824 --> 00:49:56.677
- Why are my pants cold and wet?
- Ew.

1115
00:49:56.827 --> 00:49:58.270
Uh...

1116
00:49:59.246 --> 00:49:59.938
<i>Hull breach.</i>

1117
00:50:00.080 --> 00:50:01.272
The walls are crying!

1118
00:50:01.415 --> 00:50:03.609
We're coming apart at the seams!

1119
00:50:04.793 --> 00:50:06.315
This is not how Batman dies.

1120
00:50:07.421 --> 00:50:08.522
Emmet!

1121
00:50:08.672 --> 00:50:10.615
- Hold on, hold on!
- Wyldstyle!

1122
00:50:12.551 --> 00:50:14.571
Deep breath! Deep
breath, everybod...!

1123
00:50:32.238 --> 00:50:35.433
Micro-managers, what's
going on down there?

1124
00:50:36.116 --> 00:50:38.264
Scanning submarine wreckage.

1125
00:50:39.245 --> 00:50:41.439
No survivors detected.

1126
00:50:41.580 --> 00:50:44.684
Scuba cops, dredge the
entire ocean if you have to.

1127
00:50:44.833 --> 00:50:46.856
We have got to find that Piece.

1128
00:50:47.002 --> 00:50:49.070
Let's get these prisoners
back to Lord Business...

1129
00:50:49.213 --> 00:50:50.565
and give him the good news.

1130
00:50:50.714 --> 00:50:53.533
The Special is no more.

1131
00:50:57.805 --> 00:50:59.202
Hello, everybody!

1132
00:50:59.348 --> 00:51:02.327
Superman. Wonder Woman,
I had no idea you'd be here.

1133
00:51:02.476 --> 00:51:03.873
Mr. Shaquille O'Neal.

1134
00:51:04.019 --> 00:51:05.962
Greetings, all!

1135
00:51:06.105 --> 00:51:08.458
Welcome to my Think Tank.

1136
00:51:08.774 --> 00:51:10.797
Help us!

1137
00:51:10.943 --> 00:51:13.152
All the MasterBuilders you've
captured over the years...

1138
00:51:13.153 --> 00:51:14.279
you've brought them here.

1139
00:51:14.280 --> 00:51:16.929
You're a very perceptive
person, Superman.

1140
00:51:17.074 --> 00:51:20.474
They come up with all the instructions
for everything in the universe.

1141
00:51:20.744 --> 00:51:21.720
Robots!

1142
00:51:21.870 --> 00:51:24.268
No! No! Grr!

1143
00:51:28.460 --> 00:51:30.062
Can't get much worse than this.

1144
00:51:30.212 --> 00:51:32.485
- Uh, hello, neighbor.
- Oh, no.

1145
00:51:32.631 --> 00:51:33.653
It's Green Lantern.

1146
00:51:33.799 --> 00:51:36.994
Oh, my gosh, we're roommates!
How crazy is that?

1147
00:51:37.136 --> 00:51:39.864
Does anyone have some Kryptonite
that they could give me?

1148
00:51:40.472 --> 00:51:43.451
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Where is The Special?

1149
00:51:43.601 --> 00:51:46.625
The Special and the Piece of Resistance
are at the bottom of the ocean.

1150
00:51:46.770 --> 00:51:48.622
Wait, are you telling me
you don't have him?

1151
00:51:48.772 --> 00:51:52.502
Sir, my scuba team is looking
for his remains as we speak.

1152
00:51:52.651 --> 00:51:56.722
Bad Cop, he could still be alive!
The Piece could still be out there.

1153
00:51:56.864 --> 00:52:00.434
The only remnant of The Special
was a double-decker couch.

1154
00:52:00.618 --> 00:52:01.970
Wait, hold on.

1155
00:52:02.119 --> 00:52:04.096
A double-decker couch?

1156
00:52:04.246 --> 00:52:04.892
Yes, sir.

1157
00:52:05.039 --> 00:52:09.064
Really? So it's like a bunk-bed couch?
Is that what it's like?

1158
00:52:09.209 --> 00:52:10.526
That's weird.

1159
00:52:10.669 --> 00:52:12.289
If you're sitting in
the top middle...

1160
00:52:12.421 --> 00:52:14.797
how are you gonna get down
without climbing over someone?

1161
00:52:14.798 --> 00:52:17.276
<i>If you're sitting on the bottom
and you're watching TV...</i>

1162
00:52:17.426 --> 00:52:20.154
<i>are you gonna have to watch
through a bunch of dangling legs?</i>

1163
00:52:20.304 --> 00:52:22.156
<i>Who's gonna want to
sit on the bottom?</i>

1164
00:52:22.306 --> 00:52:23.658
<i>It is literally...</i>

1165
00:52:23.807 --> 00:52:27.912
<i>the most useless idea
I have ever heard.</i>

1166
00:52:30.814 --> 00:52:33.133
- Well, we're still alive.
- Yeah!

1167
00:52:33.275 --> 00:52:35.548
Heh. The double-decker couch.

1168
00:52:35.694 --> 00:52:37.512
It wasn't totally
pointless after all.

1169
00:52:37.655 --> 00:52:39.598
It's the one thing
that stayed together.

1170
00:52:39.740 --> 00:52:41.592
I always believed in you, Emmet.

1171
00:52:41.742 --> 00:52:44.641
I don't mean to spoil the party,
but does anyone else notice...

1172
00:52:44.787 --> 00:52:47.106
we're stuck in the middle
of the ocean on this couch?

1173
00:52:47.247 --> 00:52:49.224
I mean, it's not like a
big gigantic ship...

1174
00:52:49.375 --> 00:52:50.852
is gonna come out of
nowhere and save us...

1175
00:52:51.001 --> 00:52:52.193
My gosh!

1176
00:52:56.298 --> 00:52:58.366
Avast, mateys!

1177
00:53:05.432 --> 00:53:08.331
Metal Beard, I thought you
said we were a lost cause!

1178
00:53:08.477 --> 00:53:09.578
Ye are!

1179
00:53:09.728 --> 00:53:11.705
Did ye not hear me whole story...

1180
00:53:11.855 --> 00:53:15.175
circumscribing the folly
of this whole enterprise?

1181
00:53:15.317 --> 00:53:17.761
Well, it's kind of hard not to hear
when you're yelling everything.

1182
00:53:17.903 --> 00:53:19.425
So why did you come back?

1183
00:53:19.571 --> 00:53:22.049
This be-doubled land couch.

1184
00:53:23.075 --> 00:53:26.975
I watched Lord Business'
forces completely overlook it.

1185
00:53:27.121 --> 00:53:29.349
Which means we need
more ideas like it!

1186
00:53:29.498 --> 00:53:30.269
Oh, thank you.

1187
00:53:30.416 --> 00:53:32.439
Ideas so dumb and bad...

1188
00:53:32.584 --> 00:53:36.564
that no one would ever think
they could possibly be useful.

1189
00:53:36.714 --> 00:53:38.407
Oh. Thank you.

1190
00:53:38.549 --> 00:53:41.198
So, Special, what do we do?

1191
00:53:44.430 --> 00:53:46.282
Uh...

1192
00:53:47.224 --> 00:53:48.541
Well...

1193
00:53:48.892 --> 00:53:52.917
what's the last thing Lord Business
expects MasterBuilders will do?

1194
00:53:53.063 --> 00:53:53.883
Build a spaceship?

1195
00:53:53.939 --> 00:53:54.639
Kill a chicken?

1196
00:53:54.690 --> 00:53:55.632
Marry a marshmallow.

1197
00:53:55.774 --> 00:53:56.466
Why, this:

1198
00:53:56.608 --> 00:54:00.212
<i>How you gonna keep 'em
down on the farm?</i>

1199
00:54:00.362 --> 00:54:03.341
No! It's follow the instructions.

1200
00:54:04.616 --> 00:54:06.037
- Don't like that.
- Sounds weird.

1201
00:54:06.076 --> 00:54:08.099
Now, listen. Wait, listen.

1202
00:54:10.205 --> 00:54:14.026
Guys, you're all so
talented and imaginative.

1203
00:54:14.501 --> 00:54:17.605
But you can't work
together as a team.

1204
00:54:18.630 --> 00:54:20.732
I'm just a construction worker.

1205
00:54:20.883 --> 00:54:23.953
But when I had a plan and we
were all working together...

1206
00:54:24.094 --> 00:54:26.743
I mean, we could
build a skyscraper.

1207
00:54:28.766 --> 00:54:31.585
Now, you're MasterBuilders.

1208
00:54:31.727 --> 00:54:35.832
Just imagine what could
happen if you did that.

1209
00:54:37.065 --> 00:54:39.213
You could save the universe.

1210
00:54:39.610 --> 00:54:42.384
Well said, Emmet. Well said.

1211
00:54:42.738 --> 00:54:43.634
Really?

1212
00:54:43.781 --> 00:54:46.179
She be a fine speech there, laddie.

1213
00:54:46.700 --> 00:54:47.801
Okay.

1214
00:54:49.411 --> 00:54:51.764
Somebody get me some markers...

1215
00:54:53.499 --> 00:54:55.601
some construction paper...

1216
00:54:57.711 --> 00:55:00.439
and some glitter glue!

1217
00:55:03.217 --> 00:55:04.193
I call this:

1218
00:55:04.343 --> 00:55:06.537
"Emmet's plan to get
inside the Tower...

1219
00:55:06.678 --> 00:55:08.429
put the Piece of Resistance
on the Kragle...

1220
00:55:08.430 --> 00:55:09.998
and save the world."

1221
00:55:10.140 --> 00:55:12.413
I've built a hundred just
like them back in the city.

1222
00:55:12.768 --> 00:55:15.371
If we can just get in, I know where
the air ducts and wiring are located.

1223
00:55:15.521 --> 00:55:16.543
I can get us anywhere.

1224
00:55:16.688 --> 00:55:18.005
How will we get inside?

1225
00:55:18.607 --> 00:55:19.833
In a spaceship.

1226
00:55:19.983 --> 00:55:22.677
- Spaceship! Ha, ha!
- Great idea. A Bat-Spaceship.

1227
00:55:22.820 --> 00:55:25.048
No, they're expecting
us to show up...

1228
00:55:25.197 --> 00:55:28.517
in a Bat-Spaceship, or a pirate spaceship
or a rainbow-sparkle spaceship.

1229
00:55:28.659 --> 00:55:30.034
One of those sounds awesome to me.

1230
00:55:30.035 --> 00:55:32.183
My idea is to build a spaceship...

1231
00:55:32.329 --> 00:55:35.103
that's exactly like all the other
Octan delivery spaceships.

1232
00:55:35.249 --> 00:55:38.523
So not the special spaceship that I'm
building for all of you right now?

1233
00:55:38.669 --> 00:55:40.146
Sorry, Benny. Maybe next time.

1234
00:55:40.295 --> 00:55:43.274
Ooh, you're really letting the
oxygen out of my tank here.

1235
00:55:44.550 --> 00:55:46.690
Yeah, but according to your
precious instructions...

1236
00:55:46.718 --> 00:55:48.320
this ship needs a hyperdrive.

1237
00:55:48.470 --> 00:55:49.530
We don't have that part.

1238
00:55:49.596 --> 00:55:50.656
Maybe we could find one!

1239
00:55:50.681 --> 00:55:53.432
What do you think, a spaceship is
just gonna appear out of the blue?

1240
00:55:53.433 --> 00:55:54.625
Are you kidding me?

1241
00:55:54.768 --> 00:55:55.960
The same thing!

1242
00:56:00.816 --> 00:56:01.508
- Chewie!
- Mm!

1243
00:56:01.650 --> 00:56:04.128
We're supposed to be halfway
to Naboo for a sweet party!

1244
00:56:04.278 --> 00:56:06.051
This hyperdrive keeps
malfunctioning...

1245
00:56:06.196 --> 00:56:08.094
<i>taking us to loser
systems like this.</i>

1246
00:56:08.240 --> 00:56:09.887
Captain Solo, we must go.

1247
00:56:10.033 --> 00:56:12.076
You know how perturbed I get
if we are not punctual.

1248
00:56:12.077 --> 00:56:13.554
The Droid's right. Let's roll.

1249
00:56:13.704 --> 00:56:15.431
Now hold on, Han.

1250
00:56:15.581 --> 00:56:18.104
This might be the right
galaxy after all.

1251
00:56:18.250 --> 00:56:20.648
Because I see a heavenly body.

1252
00:56:20.794 --> 00:56:24.398
Ooh, whoa, I have a boyfriend.
And it is super serious. Right, babe?

1253
00:56:24.548 --> 00:56:25.991
- Of course it's serious.
- Yeah!

1254
00:56:26.133 --> 00:56:28.156
- Got room for just one dude?
- Whoa! Babe!

1255
00:56:28.302 --> 00:56:30.450
If he's a cool dude like you.

1256
00:56:30.596 --> 00:56:31.817
You're trying to bail on us!

1257
00:56:31.930 --> 00:56:32.656
I'm not trying to bail!

1258
00:56:32.806 --> 00:56:34.658
You asked them if you could go
with them on their party ship!

1259
00:56:34.808 --> 00:56:36.350
That thing is filled
with bon vivants.

1260
00:56:36.351 --> 00:56:37.293
You speak French now?

1261
00:56:37.436 --> 00:56:40.665
Babe, look, if this relationship
is ever gonna work between us...

1262
00:56:40.814 --> 00:56:42.291
I need to feel free to party...

1263
00:56:42.441 --> 00:56:44.483
with a bunch of strangers
whenever I feel like it.

1264
00:56:44.484 --> 00:56:45.085
What?

1265
00:56:45.235 --> 00:56:46.052
Babe!

1266
00:56:47.404 --> 00:56:49.097
I will text you.

1267
00:56:49.239 --> 00:56:52.559
Where'd you get that sweet
space cape, brother?

1268
00:56:53.368 --> 00:56:55.812
It's party time!

1269
00:56:56.747 --> 00:56:57.939
Babe?

1270
00:57:06.924 --> 00:57:10.198
Wyldstyle, you're such
an amazing person.

1271
00:57:10.344 --> 00:57:14.449
And, you know, if Batman can't
see that, then he's just...

1272
00:57:14.598 --> 00:57:18.703
Well, he's just as
blind as a guy...

1273
00:57:19.186 --> 00:57:21.835
whose eyes stopped working.

1274
00:57:22.981 --> 00:57:24.628
And I'm gonna tell you something:

1275
00:57:24.775 --> 00:57:27.219
Batman is the worst
person I've ever met.

1276
00:57:27.361 --> 00:57:29.213
- Need a hyperdrive?
- No way.

1277
00:57:29.363 --> 00:57:31.090
- Babe!
- I knew it! I knew that.

1278
00:57:31.239 --> 00:57:32.591
You really had me there!

1279
00:57:32.741 --> 00:57:35.594
Those guys were so lame. All they
did was play space checkers.

1280
00:57:35.744 --> 00:57:37.642
Plus, it turns out the
hairy one's a dude.

1281
00:57:37.788 --> 00:57:39.435
And the metal one too. All dudes.

1282
00:57:39.581 --> 00:57:41.649
But won't they notice their
hyperdrive is missing?

1283
00:57:41.792 --> 00:57:44.987
Come on, Chewie,
hit the hyperdrive.

1284
00:57:47.422 --> 00:57:49.115
Nah, they'll be fine.

1285
00:57:53.470 --> 00:57:56.915
All right, we need a red
four-piece unit over at the...

1286
00:57:57.057 --> 00:57:57.749
Unikitty...

1287
00:57:57.891 --> 00:58:01.086
you're supposed to follow
the instructions, remember?

1288
00:58:01.228 --> 00:58:01.954
Sorry.

1289
00:58:02.104 --> 00:58:03.456
Ugh, this gives me the jeebies.

1290
00:58:03.605 --> 00:58:05.252
What do I even...? I can't...!

1291
00:58:08.360 --> 00:58:09.632
Nice!

1292
00:58:11.071 --> 00:58:12.593
<i>We pilot the ship to the
service entrance...</i>

1293
00:58:12.739 --> 00:58:14.762
<i>so we can get past the dangerous...</i>

1294
00:58:14.908 --> 00:58:16.385
<i>but also kind of cool...</i>

1295
00:58:16.535 --> 00:58:17.682
<i>laser gate.</i>

1296
00:58:18.620 --> 00:58:19.516
Space ID.

1297
00:58:19.663 --> 00:58:20.685
I have a drive-on.

1298
00:58:20.831 --> 00:58:22.148
Who are you here to see?

1299
00:58:22.290 --> 00:58:23.812
I'm here to see Your Butt.

1300
00:58:23.959 --> 00:58:26.437
Is that last name "Butt," first
name "Your," or is it...?

1301
00:58:26.586 --> 00:58:27.278
Oh, my gosh!

1302
00:58:30.257 --> 00:58:33.031
Pow. Wham. Ka-zap.

1303
00:58:37.264 --> 00:58:38.411
First try!

1304
00:58:39.516 --> 00:58:42.745
<i>Step three: We break into
Lord Business' office...</i>

1305
00:58:42.894 --> 00:58:45.417
<i>and we'll plunder his collection
of relics for disguises.</i>

1306
00:58:46.273 --> 00:58:47.169
<i>Step four:</i>

1307
00:58:47.315 --> 00:58:48.632
<i>Benny and Metal Beard...</i>

1308
00:58:48.775 --> 00:58:50.172
<i>will sneak their way into
the master control room.</i>

1309
00:58:50.318 --> 00:58:52.512
<i>Motion sensors triggered
in Sector 12.</i>

1310
00:58:52.654 --> 00:58:53.380
10-4.

1311
00:58:54.072 --> 00:58:54.764
Uh-oh.

1312
00:58:59.036 --> 00:59:01.309
- Are you thinking what I'm thinking?
- Oh!

1313
00:59:01.455 --> 00:59:02.772
Do it.

1314
00:59:07.252 --> 00:59:08.552
Metal Beard, that was awesome!

1315
00:59:08.628 --> 00:59:10.446
First law of the sea...

1316
00:59:10.589 --> 00:59:13.863
<i>never place your rear
end on a pirate's face.</i>

1317
00:59:14.009 --> 00:59:16.385
<i>Once inside, they'll use
their technical know-how...</i>

1318
00:59:16.386 --> 00:59:17.766
<i>to disable the Kragle shield.</i>

1319
00:59:17.888 --> 00:59:18.955
<i>I am the computer.</i>

1320
00:59:19.097 --> 00:59:21.370
Cool! Talking computer.

1321
00:59:21.516 --> 00:59:24.790
Please disable the shield systems.

1322
00:59:24.936 --> 00:59:26.162
<i>Of course.</i>

1323
00:59:26.563 --> 00:59:28.791
<i>There are no movies in
your area with that title.</i>

1324
00:59:31.068 --> 00:59:33.466
<i>Vitruvius will provide lookout and
make sure we're not being followed.</i>

1325
00:59:33.612 --> 00:59:34.838
Okay.

1326
00:59:35.363 --> 00:59:38.057
<i>Step six: Batman and Unikitty
go into the boardroom...</i>

1327
00:59:38.200 --> 00:59:40.553
<i>to make one last change
to Lord Business' plan.</i>

1328
00:59:40.702 --> 00:59:43.555
I move that we freeze the universe.
Can I get a second on that?

1329
00:59:43.705 --> 00:59:44.476
I second.

1330
00:59:44.623 --> 00:59:47.192
Bruce Wayne,
CEO of Wayne Enterprises.

1331
00:59:47.334 --> 00:59:50.028
Bruce Wayne? Uh, who's that?

1332
00:59:50.170 --> 00:59:52.489
Sounds like a cool guy.

1333
00:59:54.382 --> 00:59:55.841
We'd like to invest
in your company.

1334
00:59:55.842 --> 00:59:58.491
Your weapon to control the
universe sounds super sweet...

1335
00:59:58.678 --> 01:00:00.906
- ...I must say.
- It is, indeed, super sweet.

1336
01:00:01.056 --> 01:00:03.659
Cool. What kind of sound
system does it have?

1337
01:00:03.809 --> 01:00:06.708
Uh, sound system? Well, I mean,
we have an iPod Shuffle.

1338
01:00:06.853 --> 01:00:07.875
Wait a second.

1339
01:00:08.021 --> 01:00:09.998
You're telling me you have a
machine to control the universe...

1340
01:00:10.148 --> 01:00:12.248
and you can't listen to
tunes in surround sound?

1341
01:00:12.359 --> 01:00:13.381
Embarrassing.

1342
01:00:13.527 --> 01:00:14.594
Well, I mean...

1343
01:00:14.736 --> 01:00:17.037
we need to get that done.
I want eight-foot speakers.

1344
01:00:17.072 --> 01:00:17.843
Great call.

1345
01:00:17.989 --> 01:00:21.138
Yeah, I want speakers that you can
hug with your arms and your legs...

1346
01:00:21.284 --> 01:00:22.931
and just feel the beat.

1347
01:00:23.870 --> 01:00:27.520
Listen up! We need new instructions
for a speaker system for the TAKOS.

1348
01:00:27.666 --> 01:00:28.688
We'll never help.

1349
01:00:28.834 --> 01:00:29.935
Whatever you say, boss.

1350
01:00:30.919 --> 01:00:32.566
<i>Then once the instructions
are printed...</i>

1351
01:00:32.712 --> 01:00:34.906
<i>Wyldstyle and I will
enter the Kragle room...</i>

1352
01:00:35.048 --> 01:00:36.900
<i>place the thing on
the other thing...</i>

1353
01:00:37.050 --> 01:00:38.948
<i>and save the universe.</i>

1354
01:00:39.094 --> 01:00:41.714
Whoa, Whoa, whoa. Hey, I didn't
draw that. Is that me exploding?

1355
01:00:41.847 --> 01:00:43.449
Uh, I didn't mention that earlier?

1356
01:00:43.598 --> 01:00:46.577
When you reunite the Piece with
the Kragle, it might explode?

1357
01:00:46.726 --> 01:00:48.624
No! But it might not, right?

1358
01:00:49.688 --> 01:00:52.257
Sure, sure, sure.
Let's go with that.

1359
01:00:52.566 --> 01:00:55.135
Attention, everybody!
Incoming speaker delivery!

1360
01:01:03.577 --> 01:01:04.803
Ow!

1361
01:01:05.495 --> 01:01:06.517
Who are you two?

1362
01:01:06.663 --> 01:01:08.982
We are transfers from downstairs.

1363
01:01:09.124 --> 01:01:10.146
- What?
- Excuse me?

1364
01:01:10.292 --> 01:01:13.294
Your robot voice sounds an
awful lot like a human voice.

1365
01:01:13.295 --> 01:01:15.397
Give me a break. I've never
been a robot before.

1366
01:01:15.547 --> 01:01:17.695
What do you mean? You
have always been a robot!

1367
01:01:17.841 --> 01:01:19.818
No, no, no, do not listen to her.

1368
01:01:19.968 --> 01:01:21.820
What are your robot serial numbers?

1369
01:01:28.602 --> 01:01:30.045
<i>Everything is awesome</i>

1370
01:01:30.937 --> 01:01:32.755
No way. This is my jam.

1371
01:01:32.898 --> 01:01:34.591
This is also my jam.

1372
01:01:34.733 --> 01:01:36.551
<i>Everything is awesome</i>

1373
01:01:36.693 --> 01:01:38.921
<i>Everything is cool
When you're part of a team</i>

1374
01:01:39.070 --> 01:01:41.851
- Needs great harmonies.
- I don't want to sing the song. I'm not...

1375
01:01:41.948 --> 01:01:44.346
<i>Everything is awesome</i>

1376
01:01:44.910 --> 01:01:48.014
<i>Everything is cool
When you're part of a team</i>

1377
01:01:48.163 --> 01:01:50.607
<i>Everything is awesome</i>

1378
01:01:50.749 --> 01:01:53.523
<i>When we're living our dream</i>

1379
01:01:54.002 --> 01:01:55.149
Quick, let's go.

1380
01:01:55.295 --> 01:01:56.647
<i>Everything is awesome</i>

1381
01:01:56.796 --> 01:01:58.614
Hmm, I thought you
didn't like that song.

1382
01:01:58.757 --> 01:01:59.824
I don't.

1383
01:02:00.217 --> 01:02:01.534
Mm-hm.

1384
01:02:02.761 --> 01:02:04.363
I know you put on this tough act...

1385
01:02:04.512 --> 01:02:06.080
but I don't think you're as
mean as you're trying to seem.

1386
01:02:06.223 --> 01:02:07.666
I'm not mean.
What are you talking about?

1387
01:02:07.807 --> 01:02:10.660
I'm just saying, you were all,
"He's not The Special, Vitruvius.

1388
01:02:10.810 --> 01:02:13.709
He can't possibly be The Special.
This guy? Are you kidding me?"

1389
01:02:15.065 --> 01:02:17.418
Anyways, I don't think that's you.

1390
01:02:17.651 --> 01:02:19.344
The real you, anyway.

1391
01:02:27.369 --> 01:02:29.221
Look, Emmet.

1392
01:02:30.288 --> 01:02:32.561
I wanted it to be me, okay?

1393
01:02:33.667 --> 01:02:35.360
I wanted to be The Special.

1394
01:02:35.877 --> 01:02:39.481
And I know that sounds
super mature. It's just...

1395
01:02:39.965 --> 01:02:43.239
ever since I heard the prophecy,
I wanted to be the One.

1396
01:02:44.261 --> 01:02:46.739
<i>I was right there in that
construction site...</i>

1397
01:02:47.264 --> 01:02:49.412
<i>right on top of it, and then...</i>

1398
01:02:50.892 --> 01:02:52.369
<i>it turned out to be you.</i>

1399
01:02:58.984 --> 01:03:02.179
That night in the city, when you
thought I was The Special...

1400
01:03:05.365 --> 01:03:08.514
and you said I was
talented and important...

1401
01:03:09.786 --> 01:03:12.730
that was the first time anyone
had ever really told me that.

1402
01:03:13.707 --> 01:03:15.567
And it made me wanna do
everything I could...

1403
01:03:15.709 --> 01:03:17.652
to be the guy you
were talking about.

1404
01:03:21.131 --> 01:03:22.073
Lucy.

1405
01:03:22.215 --> 01:03:23.487
What?

1406
01:03:24.050 --> 01:03:25.993
That was my real name.

1407
01:03:26.136 --> 01:03:28.785
You asked earlier, and it's...

1408
01:03:29.889 --> 01:03:31.161
Lucy.

1409
01:03:34.644 --> 01:03:36.166
I really like that name.

1410
01:03:40.191 --> 01:03:40.883
Hey.

1411
01:03:41.026 --> 01:03:43.049
- What are you two losers talking about?
- Huh? What? Oh, nothing.

1412
01:03:43.194 --> 01:03:46.047
Thought I'd help you guys.
Left the weird cat thing to stall.

1413
01:03:46.197 --> 01:03:48.345
<i>Business, business, business.
Numbers.</i>

1414
01:03:48.491 --> 01:03:50.271
- Is this working?
- Yes.

1415
01:03:50.410 --> 01:03:51.261
Yay!

1416
01:03:51.411 --> 01:03:52.808
There's Bad Cop.

1417
01:03:53.788 --> 01:03:56.641
<i>Oh, Danny boy, the pipes...</i>

1418
01:03:56.791 --> 01:03:58.643
Okay. Wait for my signal.

1419
01:03:58.793 --> 01:04:00.315
Good luck, Emmet.

1420
01:04:00.712 --> 01:04:01.813
Lucy.

1421
01:04:03.006 --> 01:04:04.779
I guess this might be goodbye.

1422
01:04:05.216 --> 01:04:08.411
I don't like goodbyes.
Let's just call this:

1423
01:04:08.762 --> 01:04:10.739
"See you later, alligator."

1424
01:04:11.306 --> 01:04:13.625
"See you later, alligator"?

1425
01:04:15.435 --> 01:04:17.629
After a while, crocodile.

1426
01:04:20.774 --> 01:04:21.841
Who's Lucy?

1427
01:04:21.983 --> 01:04:23.505
Batman, when we get
inside this room...

1428
01:04:23.651 --> 01:04:25.219
there are gonna be audio
sensors everywhere.

1429
01:04:25.362 --> 01:04:27.339
We have to be really, really quiet.

1430
01:04:27.489 --> 01:04:30.513
Don't worry, Dad, I read your dumb
instructions. Stop yelling at me.

1431
01:04:30.658 --> 01:04:32.055
Benny, what's our
status with the shield?

1432
01:04:32.202 --> 01:04:33.542
Oh, yeah, no, it's going great.

1433
01:04:33.578 --> 01:04:36.056
It's just going great, if
somebody would listen to me!

1434
01:04:36.206 --> 01:04:38.434
<i>Downloading latest episode
of Where Are My Pants?</i>

1435
01:04:38.583 --> 01:04:41.186
<i>Where are you getting "pants" from?
You know what I want!</i>

1436
01:04:41.336 --> 01:04:42.483
<i>The pipes are calling...</i>

1437
01:04:43.463 --> 01:04:44.189
Bad Cop.

1438
01:04:44.339 --> 01:04:46.237
<i>Hi, this is Lord
Business' assistant.</i>

1439
01:04:46.383 --> 01:04:48.523
<i>He would like you to come
to his office immediately.</i>

1440
01:04:48.551 --> 01:04:49.371
Copy that.

1441
01:04:49.427 --> 01:04:51.370
- Thanks.
- You are welcome, sir.

1442
01:04:54.599 --> 01:04:55.700
Hey, who is that?

1443
01:04:58.853 --> 01:04:59.954
That's the signal...

1444
01:05:00.105 --> 01:05:02.128
but the shield is still up.

1445
01:05:02.273 --> 01:05:03.716
We'll wing it.

1446
01:05:04.776 --> 01:05:06.719
That's a bat pun.

1447
01:05:08.863 --> 01:05:09.964
Shh. Benny...

1448
01:05:10.115 --> 01:05:11.683
disable the shield.

1449
01:05:11.825 --> 01:05:12.906
<i>- Disable the shield.</i>
- Now.

1450
01:05:13.118 --> 01:05:14.265
Disable the shield.

1451
01:05:14.411 --> 01:05:16.271
<i>- Searching for Albanian restaurants.</i>
- What?

1452
01:05:16.329 --> 01:05:19.540
- No! I never once said anything...!
<i>- I don't understand what you mean.</i>

1453
01:05:19.541 --> 01:05:20.767
<i>Disable the shield!</i>

1454
01:05:20.917 --> 01:05:21.984
Benny, what's going on?

1455
01:05:22.127 --> 01:05:23.695
<i>Disable the shield! Come on!</i>

1456
01:05:23.837 --> 01:05:25.405
You are undermining me!

1457
01:05:25.547 --> 01:05:27.490
<i>Which phrase would you
like me to underline?</i>

1458
01:05:27.632 --> 01:05:28.779
Disable the shield!

1459
01:05:28.925 --> 01:05:30.242
Let me try.

1460
01:05:30.468 --> 01:05:34.573
Be ye disabling of yon shield.

1461
01:05:34.722 --> 01:05:35.539
<i>Disabling shield.</i>

1462
01:05:35.682 --> 01:05:36.408
What?

1463
01:05:40.270 --> 01:05:42.919
Okay, in three...

1464
01:05:44.524 --> 01:05:45.466
two...

1465
01:05:46.985 --> 01:05:48.086
one.

1466
01:05:49.320 --> 01:05:50.888
Let's do this.

1467
01:05:52.157 --> 01:05:53.053
Lucy!

1468
01:05:56.286 --> 01:05:56.887
Lucy!

1469
01:05:58.580 --> 01:05:59.681
No!

1470
01:06:01.124 --> 01:06:02.567
Oh, man.

1471
01:06:02.834 --> 01:06:04.026
Oh, no.

1472
01:06:04.502 --> 01:06:05.194
Uh-oh.

1473
01:06:05.503 --> 01:06:08.356
<i>Sneaking around the corner...</i>

1474
01:06:10.049 --> 01:06:11.947
- Unh!
- Vitruvius.

1475
01:06:12.093 --> 01:06:15.618
I see you've accidentally
wandered into my Think Tank.

1476
01:06:15.763 --> 01:06:18.036
And by the way, I found
a few of your friends.

1477
01:06:18.183 --> 01:06:21.162
- By which I mean all of them!
- Sorry!

1478
01:06:21.311 --> 01:06:23.084
Acceptable work, Bad Cop.

1479
01:06:23.229 --> 01:06:24.000
Thank you, sir.

1480
01:06:24.147 --> 01:06:26.841
Robots, destroy this
old man at once.

1481
01:06:26.983 --> 01:06:28.380
Did you just call me "old"?

1482
01:06:28.526 --> 01:06:29.843
Yeah. So what?

1483
01:06:30.487 --> 01:06:33.636
Well, Junebug, I really
prefer the word...

1484
01:06:33.781 --> 01:06:34.882
"experienced"!

1485
01:06:50.798 --> 01:06:51.694
Aha.

1486
01:06:51.841 --> 01:06:52.737
You see, Emmet?

1487
01:06:52.884 --> 01:06:56.204
A corrupted spirit is no match
for the purity of imagina...

1488
01:06:59.766 --> 01:07:01.066
- Ha-ha-ha!
- Vitruvius!

1489
01:07:01.100 --> 01:07:02.668
No!

1490
01:07:04.896 --> 01:07:05.997
Vitruvius.

1491
01:07:07.148 --> 01:07:10.172
My sweet Emmet. Come closer.

1492
01:07:10.360 --> 01:07:12.758
You must know something
about the prophecy.

1493
01:07:12.904 --> 01:07:14.756
I know, I'm doing my best...

1494
01:07:14.906 --> 01:07:15.723
but I don't...

1495
01:07:15.865 --> 01:07:17.387
The prophecy...

1496
01:07:17.909 --> 01:07:19.135
I made it up.

1497
01:07:19.536 --> 01:07:20.683
What?

1498
01:07:21.120 --> 01:07:23.894
I made it up. It's not true.

1499
01:07:24.666 --> 01:07:26.393
But that means I'm just...

1500
